\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MORNING BRIEFING: Hungarian Flood, Czech Data in Focus\b0\par\par\uc2 539 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 2013\par 04:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR \par Local/GMT \par   N/A Flood situation in Budapest \par   0900/0700 Czech May inflation data \par   0900/0700 Czech May unemployment data \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hungary has declared a national emergency after the River Danube topped its highest recorded levels in Budapest Monday. Soldiers and civilian volunteers have been pressed into service to build dams out of sandbags.\f28 \par \par \uc2 In the Czech Republic, the focus will continue to be on clean-up following severe flooding.\par \par \uc2 Czech inflation is expected to continue dropping in May, due to falling energy prices, enabling the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain its accommodative monetary policy.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par EUR/CZK \par Latest 0150 GMT 25.553-89 \par Previous 2150 GMT 25.517-606 \par %Chg +0.04 \par  \par EUR/HUF \par Latest 0150 GMT 295.39-6.22 \par Previous 2150 GMT 294.67-5.79 \par % Chg +0.19 \par EUR/PLN \par Latest 0150 GMT 4.2367-470 \par Previous 2150 GMT 4.2286-500 \par % Chg +0.06 \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par Hungary \par          Fri   Thu \par 3 yrs   4.75%  4.75% \par 5 yrs   5.30%  5.35% \par 10yrs   5.85%  5.90% \par  \par Poland \par          Fri   Thu \par 3 yrs   2.83%  2.85%(1) \par 5 yrs   3.26%  3.30% \par 10yrs   3.73%  3.73% \par (1) 2 yrs \par  \par Czech Republic \par          Fri   Thu \par 3 yrs   0.50%  0.50% \par 5 yrs   1.25%  1.24% \par 10yrs   2.07%  2.08%(1) \par (1) 11 yrs \par  \par STOCKS \par  \par WIG 20 \par  957.45 +0.72 +0.08% \par  \par BUX \par 19,632.63 +428.93 +2.23% \par  \par PX \par  2,488.84 +42.55 +1.74% \par  \par OTHER NEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CZECH REPUBLIC: The Czech government will meet its goal to lower its budget deficit below 3% of the country's total economic output this year despite floods wreaking havoc across many areas last week and heavy thunderstorms causing localized flash floods over the weekend, Prime Minister Petr Necas said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We will stick to our strategy to maintain the deficit of public finances at below 3%," Mr. Necas said Sunday in a live interview on the Czech public television news broadcaster CT24.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 POLAND\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may again \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to limit the Polish zloty's volatility, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Marek Belka told state news agency PAP late Friday, hours after the bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market for the first time since December 2011.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: Hungary's flood defenses held firm on Sunday morning as central Europe's worst floods in a decade moved through the northwest of the country toward the capital Budapest.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thousands of emergency workers, troops and volunteers in Germany battled the flooding on Sunday which have forced evacuations and which one politician termed a "national catastrophe."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: Romania's unemployment rate edged down to 5.03% in May, from 5.29% a month earlier, the country's employment agency \f28 \uc2 \f2 ANOFM\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday, news agency Mediafax reports. In May 2012, the unemployment rate was 4.9%, \f28 \uc2 \f2 ANOFM\f28 \uc2 \f2  data showed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Marynia Kruk at marynia.kruk@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Go to \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope}}}\uc2 \f2  for the WSJ blog on Central and Eastern Europe, covering business, politics, society and more, written by our correspondents across the region. [ 06-09-13 2204ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020130610e96a0000c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
