\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3- \highlight22\uc2 Poland intervenes \highlight\uc2  to bolster zloty\b0\par\par\uc2 559 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2013\par 15:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Several \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  after zloty hit one-year low\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had earlier said weak zloty not a concern\par \par \uc2 * Zloty gains as much as two percent versus euro\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at trimming excessive volatility, c.bank head says\par \par \uc2 By Dagmara Leszkowicz\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, June 7 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday to prop up the zloty for the first time in 18 months after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a one-year low the previous session.\par \par \uc2 Over the past month, the zloty has fallen because of lower Polish interest rates and fears that the U.S. Federal Reserve could wind down its quantitative easing campaign, something which has hit emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the world.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts thought Polish officials were moved to act by concerns that a falling zloty could boost the value of the country's debts, which could trigger painful spending cuts.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it sold some foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the spot market. Dealers said it had entered the market several times and that state-owned BGK bank also stepped into the market in the late afternoon trade, helping the zloty to extend its sharp gains.\par \par \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, Marek Belka, told the state news agency PAP that the bank's move was aimed at trimming excessive fluctuation on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 "It is absolutely not a test of betting against the trend. We just had a couple of crazy days recently (on the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market) and we had to stop it," Belka said, adding that further \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are not ruled out.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumped by around 2 percent versus the euro after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move. By 1615 GMT it had given up some gains to trade at 4.2325 per euro.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time at the zloty level of 4.30 to the euro. They did not give details on the total amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or the amount of zlotys.\par \par \uc2 The bank last stepped into the market to lift the zloty in December 2011, when officials were seeking to keep the value of the government's foreign-denominated debt below a constitutionally set level of 55 percent of gross domestic product.\par \par \uc2 Breaching the level would have forced the government to reduce spending substantially.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the zloty fell to its lowest levels since June 2012 after Belka said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness was not a concern.\par \par \uc2 Rafal Benecki, chief economist at \uc2 ING Bank Slaski\uc2 , said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a surprise that contradicted the governor's statement.\par \par \uc2 "It's strange, because Belka seemed as if he had wanted to weaken the zloty on Wednesday and now they are strengthening it," Benecki said.\par \par \uc2 "The bank most likely wants to reduce the volatility of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , because there is a large risk of debt breaching the 55 percent of GDP threshold."\par \par \uc2 The ratio stood at 52.7 percent of GDP at the end of last year, according to Polish accounting rules.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  brought its main rate to a new low of 2.75 percent earlier this week, 200 basis points lower than in November, when it launched an easing campaign to help boost the flagging economy.\par \par \uc2 POLAND-ZLOTY/ (UPDATE 3) | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | BNX | PX | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130607e967000pc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
