\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ BLOG: \uc2 Polish  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Chief Wants Criterion Waived Ahead of Euro Entry\b0\par\par\uc2 490 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2013\par 16:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (This story has been posted on The Wall Street Journal Online's Emerging Europe blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope}}}\uc2 .)\par \par \uc2 By Patryk Wasilewski\par \par \uc2 WARSAW--\uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said the country should be allowed to join the euro without first putting its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the usual two-year transition in the \uc2 European Union\uc2 's exchange rate mechanism known as ERM2, which he claimed could be an open invitation to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators.\par \par \uc2 Marek Belka's comments mark the strongest call yet from a Polish official for the euro entry rules to be relaxed. Poland has the biggest economy among the ex-communist euro candidates.\par \par \uc2 Countries adopting the euro are obliged to keep their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the ERM2 grid where they must trade within a relatively narrow band for two years. Poland must also meet other fiscal and monetary criteria.\par \par \uc2 "I dislike ERM2 very much," Mr. Belka told a meeting of economists alongside President Bronislaw Komorowski on Thursday. "We should openly say that ERM2 is bad for Poland, bad for a country like Poland. The spot market in the zloty is bigger than in the Brazilian real."\par \par \uc2 Brazil's population and its economy are about five times the size of Poland's in nominal terms.\par \par \uc2 "If the Swedes wanted to join the euro for political reasons, a red carpet would be rolled out and they'd say: forget about that ERM2. I'm waiting for a moment like this for Poland," Mr. Belka said, adding the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  grid is "very dangerous" for the Polish economy because it would "invite massive speculation" in the zloty.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief is an influential voice in Poland's euro debate. On his watch the \uc2 National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times to support the zloty during the euro's debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 Poland doesn't have a target date for adopting the euro but government officials have said they would like the country to meet all the criteria by 2015 with the exception of the two-year ERM2 stint. A political decision would follow parliamentary elections set for that year.\par \par \uc2 Dropping the ERM2 condition would require a treaty change accepted by the EU's soon-to-be 28 nations. Mr. Belka said that he was aware of the obstacle but that "the EU has shown a flexible approach" to its treaties.\par \par \uc2 It doesn't look very realistic in the short term "but it doesn't mean we shouldn't talk about it," he said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  believes it will be able to keep its inflation in check to meet the price stability criterion without changing its consumer price index targeting, where it aims for annual inflation of 2.5%.\par \par \uc2 Write to Patryk Wasilewski at patryk.wasilewski@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  -For continuously updated news from The Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 \f2 . \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 04-04-13 1440GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130404e944000nb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoa