\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 1-Hungary's forint extends gains, crown firmer before cbank\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jason Hovet   \par \uc2 808 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 12:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 PRAGUE, March 27 (Reuters) - The forint climbed more against a weak euro on Wednesday after Hungary cut interest rates again but refrained from any radical easing measures, while the crown edged up on bets that the threat of Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has eased.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's zloty also edged up against the euro after Polish Prime Minister Donald Tusk dropped his objections to a referendum on joining the shared \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is trying to jumpstart a recession-hit economy, cut interest rates to a record low on Tuesday but avoided any policy surprises under its new governor, helping the forint jump almost 1 percent.\par \par \uc2 By 1004 GMT on Wednesday, the forint had risen another 0.2 percent and was bid at 303.74 to the euro.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now 1.5 percent off a 14-month low hit last week, and some say that if \uc2 Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is cautious in its policy moves it could avoid a long-term slide that would hurt the many Hungarian households and companies with loans in euros or Swiss francs.\par \par \uc2 "The press release (after the rate decision) was rather cautious and in line with expectations, which we see as a tactical way for it to gain the markets' confidence back and take some pressure off the weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," SEB said in a morning trading note.\par \par \uc2 "(The forint) can potentially reach the (record low) at 324 but our forecast is 310 in one month and end of Q2, 305 at the end of Q3, and thereafter stabilising at the 300 level."\par \par \uc2 Still, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  indicated on Wednesday it was exploring "tools" other than interest rates to aid economic growth, while underlining that any steps it takes cannot jeopardise its primary goal of keeping inflation under control.\par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Viktor Orban has picked close ally and former economy minister Gyorgy Matolcsy to head the bank with a mandate to help the economy, sparking fears it may implement unconventional measures that would weaken the forint.\par \par \uc2 All three of central Europe's bigger former communist economies have been cutting rates steadily in a bid to bolster growth as most of the euro zone falters.\par \par \uc2 Only Romania, which meets on Thursday, has stayed on hold due to inflation pressures. Analysts do not expect loosening there until later in 2013.\par \par \uc2 The Romanian leu, the Polish zloty and the crown all gained around 1 percent, with the latter bid at 25.714 to the euro.\par \par \uc2 With Czech interest rates already at "technical zero", the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be its next easing tool to help the contracting economy. But the weakening of the crown to a nine-month low in the past month has reduced those chances, analyst have said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meets on Thursday and investors will look for clues of whether more easing is ahead. Six of 21 economists said they now expected the bank to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , versus 12 who said so in February. Those who foresaw \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  generally predicted it would happen some time in the second half of this year.\par \par \uc2 "We have been testing 25.800/850 area without breaking higher, so now a bit of a correction," a Prague dealer said.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think that people expect anything exciting from tomorrow's (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) meeting with EUR/CZK at these levels."\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                    close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                             change   change\par                                             today    in 2013 \par Czech crown                  25.714    25.731  +0.07%    -2.59%\par Polish zloty                 4.176    4.18  +0.1%    -2.44%\par Hungarian forint             303.74    304.33  +0.19%    -4.21%\par Croatian kuna                7.592    7.592   0%    -0.54%\par Romanian leu                 4.402    4.408  +0.14%   +0.93%\par Serbian dinar                111.94    111.67   -0.24%   +0.32%\par Yield Spreads\par Czech treasury bonds           \par 2-yr T-bond   CZ2YT=RR   +1 basis points to  45bps over bmk*\par 7-yr T-bond   CZ6YT=RR   +2 basis points to  +92bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   CZ10YT=RR   +2 basis points to  +54bps over bmk*\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Benchmark is German bond equivalent.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 All data taken from Reuters at 1107 CET.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  percent change calculated from the daily domestic\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 close at 1700 GMT.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For related news and prices, click on the codes in brackets: All emerging market news Spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Eastern Europe spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   Middle East spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\