\par\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \b \uc2 Polish Central Bankers to Reassess Policy\b0\par\par\uc2 By Patryk Wasilewski and Gordon Fairclough   \par \uc2 553 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Februar 2013\par 17:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones Top Global Market Stories\par \uc2 DJTGMS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW--Poland's rate setters are in the process of reassessing their monetary policy options for the medium term, \uc2 Marek Belka\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, told The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 At its March sitting, the 10-member rate panel will likely choose between a cut or a pause in the easing cycle that has so far taken the benchmark rate down one percentage point to 3.75%. But the four monthly cuts made to date mean the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is close to the end of the current policy phase.\par \par \uc2 "What we need, we think, is to look at the next projections--inflation and gross domestic product projections that will be issued in a matter of weeks. Secondly, we have to look at the things we usually haven't looked at, like the situation on the treasury-bond market," Mr. Belka said. "It's not really about making a pause or not. It's about realizing that we're at a certain moment in the Polish economy, when we need to ask: what do we need now? This is something we're discussing at the moment."\par \par \uc2 Following the February rate cut, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said that a similar move in March was less of a done deal, although it kept its informal easing bias.\par \par \uc2 The Polish economy is going through a rough patch. Growth slowed to 2% last year from 4.3% in 2011, and the government has put part of the blame on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , calling cuts to borrowing costs too little too late. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  currently expects average inflation to ease to 2.5% with growth slowing further to 1.5% in 2013.\par \par \uc2 The economy is, however, expected to bottom out this year, with contraction unlikely in any quarter and growth accelerating in the second half of the year.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also has an additional factor to consider--a rally last year pushed yields on 10-year Polish government bonds sharply lower, from more than 5.6% in early 2012 to around 4% at present, with foreign investors increasing their holdings. With that comes additional risks, Mr. Belka said.\par \par \uc2 "Growing demand for Polish bonds could be interpreted as fantastic, but we're not extremely happy about the increasing share of non-residents in this market," Mr. Belka said.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors have flocked to Poland in search of higher yields, which despite all the buying remain significantly above those of many euro-zone sovereigns. The rally has pushed yields down more quickly than the \uc2 Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cut its benchmark rate, which has made the paper less attractive for Polish financial institutions.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said capital flight from Poland could destabilize the bond market as well as the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which would weaken rapidly. The \uc2 National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times in 2011 to stop investors from betting against the zloty, which was depreciating at the time. The zloty was around PLN4.19 ($1.33) to the euro on Monday afternoon, some 3% weaker than at the beginning of the year, with recent poor macroeconomic readings boosting expectations of more rate cuts.\par \par \uc2 Write to Patryk Wasilewski at patryk.wasilewski@wsj.com and Gordon Fairclough at gordon.fairclough@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJTGMS1120130219e92j0006w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
