\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MORNING BRIEFING: Poland Seen Cutting Rates, Czechs to Focus on  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sean Carney   \par \uc2 889 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 2013\par 04:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR \par Local/GMT \par N/A - Poland \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  monetary policy decision \par 1300/1200 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  monetary policy decision \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Monetary policy in the cooling Polish economy and the recession-struck Czech Republic will be in focus Wednesday, with the entrenched bias toward easing likely to result in lower rates in Warsaw and talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Prague.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to cut interest rates for the fourth time in a row, bringing the benchmark rate to 3.75% from 4%. The Polish economy sharply decelerated last year with growth slowing to 2% annually from 4.3% the previous year.\par \par \uc2 With investors and analysts already counting on an interest rate cut, the market will be looking for hints in the post-decision commentary that the rate-setting panel is ready to pause in its easing campaign.\par \par \uc2 In Prague, the \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has nowhere to go with interest rates, having cut the benchmark rate to 0.05% late last year.\par \par \uc2 But as inflation is tame and the economy has been contracting steadily since late 2011, policy makers may focus on ways to counteract slowing price growth while giving exports a boost.\par \par \uc2 Continued talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \hig