\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MORNING BRIEFING: Poland Seen Cutting Rates, Czechs to Focus on  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sean Carney   \par \uc2 889 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 2013\par 04:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR \par Local/GMT \par N/A - Poland \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  monetary policy decision \par 1300/1200 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  monetary policy decision \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Monetary policy in the cooling Polish economy and the recession-struck Czech Republic will be in focus Wednesday, with the entrenched bias toward easing likely to result in lower rates in Warsaw and talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Prague.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to cut interest rates for the fourth time in a row, bringing the benchmark rate to 3.75% from 4%. The Polish economy sharply decelerated last year with growth slowing to 2% annually from 4.3% the previous year.\par \par \uc2 With investors and analysts already counting on an interest rate cut, the market will be looking for hints in the post-decision commentary that the rate-setting panel is ready to pause in its easing campaign.\par \par \uc2 In Prague, the \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has nowhere to go with interest rates, having cut the benchmark rate to 0.05% late last year.\par \par \uc2 But as inflation is tame and the economy has been contracting steadily since late 2011, policy makers may focus on ways to counteract slowing price growth while giving exports a boost.\par \par \uc2 Continued talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also in the offing.\par \par \uc2 Last autumn, the \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued a series of verbal warnings that resulted in the koruna losing roughly 5% to the euro. For the central bankers, that easing in conditions may be sufficient, as no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has yet taken place and the warnings have become less frequent.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also due to issue its latest macroeconomic forecasts, which analysts say will likely include downward revisions to gross domestic product expectations, meaning the economy is expected to remain weaker for longer than previously expected.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par EUR/CZK \par Latest 0250 GMT 25.618-78 \par Previous 2150 GMT 25.601-78 \par %Chg +0.03 \par  \par EUR/HUF \par Latest 0250 GMT 294.49-5.04 \par Previous 2150 GMT 293.94-4.99 \par % Chg +0.10 \par  \par EUR/PLN \par Latest 0250 GMT 4.1745-864 \par Previous 2150 GMT 4.1737-816 \par % Chg +0.07 \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par Hungary \par         Tues   Mon \par 3 yrs   5.47%  5.45% \par 5 yrs   5.95%  5.95% \par 10yrs   6.40%  6.30% \par  \par Poland \par         Tues   Mon \par 3 yrs   3.23%  3.22(1) \par 5 yrs   3.41%  3.39% \par 10yrs   3.92%  3.91% \par (1) 2 yrs \par  \par Czech Republic \par         Tues   Mon \par 3 yrs   0.41%  0.41% \par 5 yrs   1.24%  1.25% \par 10yrs   1.95%  1.95% \par STOCKS \par  \par WIG 20 \par  2,485.25 +15.52 +0.63% \par  \par BUX \par 19,264.86 +174.65 +0.91% \par  \par PX \par 998.74 -8.79 -0.87% \par  \par EU Enlarged \par  1,919.82 +14.22 +0.75% \par  \par OTHER NEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: Poland's biggest gas consuming companies will derive the first benefits from market determined gas prices starting July this year, with all other businesses following a year later, the energy regulator URE said Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 From July 2014, gas trading on the recently launched commodity exchange is expected to cover about 70% of the market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: Poland's government drew a line in the sand ahead of the upcoming \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 's summit, saying proposed 30 billion euros ($39.9 billion) of additional budget cuts were "inconceivable."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EU leaders will Feb. 7-8 meet to try to agree on the size and structure of the bloc's budget for 2014-2020 after the failure of their previous attempt in November over the EUR30 billion of more cuts proposed by Germany.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: Hungary plans to double the volume of its trade with Turkey by 2015 to goods and services worth 5 billion euros ($6.79 billion), Prime Minister Viktor Orban said after talks with his Turkish counterpart Recep Tayyip Erdogan Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Orban echoed Czech Prime Minister Petr Necas's comment Monday, saying his government also fully backs Turkey's \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  bid for membership.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: Hungary's governing Fidesz party Tuesday night denied a local press report that the decision has been made to name Economy Minister Gyorgy Matolcsy as the successor to departing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Andras Simor.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Business daily Vilaggazdasag's report in its online edition earlier in the evening, which cited "a trusted source" about the matter, is unfounded and a hoax, Fidesz communication director Mate Kocsis told state news agency MTI.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Romania's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept its key interest rate unchanged at 5.25% for the seventh consecutive meeting Tuesday, in line with expectations, despite a weakening economy, news agency Mediafax reported.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also maintained the minimum reserve requirements unchanged at 15% for Romanian leu-denominated liabilities and at 20% for foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  liabilities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BULGARIA: Bulgarian investigators on Tuesday for the first time linked Shiite group Hezbollah to a deadly July bomb attack on Israeli tourists in the country and identified two of the perpetrators as residents of Lebanon traveling on Australian and Canadian passports.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Patryk Wasilewski in Warsaw contributed to this briefing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Sean Carney at sean.carney@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Go to \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope/}}}\uc2 \f2  for the WSJ blog on Central and Eastern Europe, covering business, politics, society and more, written by our correspondents across the region. [ 06-02-13 0305GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091   \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020130206e92600006\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
