\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Poland to cut rates for 4th straight month in Feb\b0\par\par\uc2 599 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2013\par 15:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * All 27 analysts polled see 25 bp rate cut on Feb.6\par \par \uc2 * Rates seen down to 3.50 pct by end-March-median\par \par \uc2 * Easing seen coming earlier as economic data disappoint\par \par \uc2 By Marcin Goettig\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Feb 1 (Reuters) - \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will cut interest rates by 25 basis points for the fourth successive month in February as a sharp economic slowdown and a drop in inflation open the way for more easing, a Reuters poll showed on Friday.\par \par \uc2 All 27 analysts polled by Reuters from Jan. 29 to Feb. 1 expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 10-strong Monetary Policy Council (MPC) to cut the key rate to 3.75 percent at the Feb. 5-6 meeting.\par \par \uc2 With inflation back below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 2.5 percent target for the first time in more than two years and retail sales in December recording their sharpest drop in eight years, analysts brought forward the expected timing of gradual rate cuts.\par \par \uc2 Now they expect the Council to cut rates again by 25 basis points in March, which would bring the key rate to 3.50 percent. Last month analysts predicted that rates would not fall to this level earlier than the end of June.\par \par \uc2 Rates in Poland have never been below 3.50 percent and the last time they were at that level was more than two years ago.\par \par \uc2 "The combination of weak growth and low inflation mean there is no reason to stick to a policy that is too restrictive," said Piotr Bielski, senior economist at \uc2 Bank Zachodni WBK\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Polish rates are still the third-highest in the \uc2 European Union\uc2  after Hungary and Romania, but as price growth has exceeded the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target for most of the past five years, many council members have favoured cautious reductions.\par \par \uc2 Economic growth fell to its weakest in three years in 2012, data showed earlier this week, signalling that one of Europe's most resilient economies risks dipping into recession.\par \par \uc2 This prompted one of the rate-setters, Anna Zielinska-Glebocka, to say a 25 basis point cut in February is a "pretty much done deal."\par \par \uc2 "The Council is following a strategy of small steps. It decided to start cutting too late and too slowly, (so) it should make two more steps," BZ WBK's Bielski added.\par \par \uc2 One of the most fervent supporters of lower rates on the MPC, Elzbieta Chojna-Duch, said this week that it was already too late for a larger cut and that the policy of gradual easing should be continued.\par \par \uc2 Following the string of disappointing data \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Marek Belka abandoned his earlier talk of a possible pause in cuts, saying instead that Poland is "in the midst of a monetary easing cycle".\par \par \uc2 On top of that, voting records have shown that even the most resolute hawks have finally backed a 25 basis point cut in December.\par \par \uc2 Poland launched a cycle of monetary easing in November, having last raised its benchmark interest rate in May.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees growth slowing to 1.5 percent this year, the lowest rate in eleven years. The bank will publish its new inflation and GDP projections in March.\par \par \uc2 Poland is lagging other countries in the region in relaxing monetary policy. Hungary cut rates for the sixth month running in January, while the \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has reduced its key rate to near zero and signals possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Marcin Goettig)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 POLAND\b0 \highlight\uc2 -RATES/ (POLL) | ABN | D | PX | E | RBN | M   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130204e921000x5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
