\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 2-Hungarian, Polish  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  firmer\b0\par\par\uc2 753 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2012\par 12:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds Hungary bond, bill auction, updates markets)\par \par \uc2 * Hungary's CPI slows in Nov, c.bank seen cutting rates\par \par \uc2 * Forint, zloty firmer, Czech crown, leu shade weaker\par \par \uc2 * Hungary flags possible \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt issue in Q1\par \par \uc2 * Romania's CPI slows, markets focus on politics\par \par \uc2 By Krisztina Than\par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST, Dec 11 (Reuters) - The Polish zloty and the forint led Eastern European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher on Tuesday and Hungarian bond yields dropped on expectations of further interest rates cuts this month.\par \par \uc2 A 3-month treasury bill auction attracted strong demand with the average yield falling to 5.77 percent from 5.96 percent at the previous auction a week ago.\par \par \uc2 Hungary, which has not tapped international markets since 2011, also flagged a possible foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bond issue in the first quarter of 2013 after talks with the IMF on a financing backstop have stalled.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's headline inflation rate slowed to an annual 5.2 percent in November from 6 percent in October, which may allow dovish rate setters to vote for a fresh rate cut at the bank's meeting next week, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 The forint rose, tracking the euro/dollar which also pushed the Polish zloty higher, dealers said. Hungarian bond yields dropped 10-20 basis points from Monday's fixing , with the 3-year bond trading at 5.70 percent.\par \par \uc2 "Inflation was expected to slow due to base effects, so this had been priced in and... the market is now expecting the next rate cut," a fixed income trader in Budapest said.\par \par \uc2 Another trader said the market was fairly illiquid.\par \par \uc2 With a majority of rate setters viewing inflation risks as manageable, the Hungarian bank has cut rates by 100 basis points since August to help the recession-hit economy.\par \par \uc2 Its peer, the \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has cut its main rate to 0.05 percent and has signalled the next tool available is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the crown, possibly next year.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also cut its key rate twice, by 25 basis points each time, pushing borrowing costs down to 4.25 percent, their lowest since May 2011.\par \par \uc2 Its Governor Marek Belka said on Tuesday the bank was "very likely" to cut rates further and he also expected inflation to return to the bank's target within months.\par \par \uc2 The zloty added half a percent on Tuesday while the forint was up 0.4 percent at 1110 GMT.\par \par \uc2 The Czech crown was 0.1 percent lower and the Romanian leu also eased a shade after a weekend election gave a clear victory to Romanian Prime Minister Victor Ponta.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                    close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                             change   change\par                                             today    in 2011 \par Czech crown                  25,272    25,243  -0.11%  +1.08%\par Polish zloty                 4,085    4,107    +0.54%  +9.29%\par Hungarian forint             281,92    283,17  +0.44%  +11.59%\par Croatian kuna                7,512    7,532   +0.27%   +0.05%\par Romanian leu                 4,54   