\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Polish Government Takes Step Toward Easing Public Debt Cap\b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2012\par 16:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 WARSAW--Poland's government Tuesday took another step towards relaxing its regulations over the ceiling on public debt by approving the finance ministry's proposals aimed at better protecting it against volatility of the Polish zloty, the government said.\par \par \uc2 The main regulation forcing Poland's government to start painful austerity measures, including spending cuts and tax increases, once public debt exceeds 55% of gross domestic product will remain in place. In 2012 public debt, calculated under Polish standards, is expected to reach 52.4% of GDP.\par \par \uc2 However, the government will now use an average annual \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate to value the country's sizeable debt pile, which will reduce the threat of breaking the key threshold due to the weakening of the zloty.\par \par \uc2 The government will be also be allowed to take from debt funds used to earlier fund next year's borrowing needs.\par \par \uc2 Existing regulations, under which the zloty rate from last day of December was used to value the foreign debt, made the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  prone to high volatility late in the year and last year forced the country's finance ministry and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  already financed more than 29 billion zlotys ($9.15 billion) of next year's borrowing needs.\par \par \uc2 The government's decision still has to be approved by the parliament, in which the governing coalition of Civic Platform and Poland's Peasants Party has a narrow majority.\par \par \uc2 Write to Patryk Wasilewski at patryk.wasilewski@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 27, 2012 10:12 ET (15:12 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020121127e8br004ft\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
