\par\par \b \uc2 NBP Belka:  \highlight22\uc2 Currency Interventions \highlight\uc2  '11 Supported  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2 's Stability\b0\par\par\uc2 172 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juli 2012\par 10:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 WARSAW--The Polish economy is internally balanced, which is the main reason for its resilience in the face of the euro zone's debt crisis, although "it's hard to be unconditionally optimistic," said Marek Belka, governor of the National Bank of Poland.\par \par \uc2 In a speech to parliament Wednesday, Mr. Belka said \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "one of the few remaining central banks in Europe" that can stick to conventional monetary policy, with positive real interest rates and an economy growing around 3% in the second quarter.\par \par \uc2 Poland's benchmark rate is 4.75%, while annual consumer price inflation was 4.3% in June.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Belka also said Poland's inflation rate will be near the bank's 1.5%-3.5% tolerance range at the end of this year and will approach its 2.5% target next year.\par \par \uc2 Write to Marcin Sobczyk at marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Subscribe to WSJ: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires }}}\uc2  [ 25-07-12 0903GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120725e87p000n3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
