\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-Polish c.bank deputy downplays need for  \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 662 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 2012\par 15:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Deputy cbank head Kozinski sees relatively stable zloty\par \par \uc2 * Cites solid Polish economy, euro zone summit deal\par \par \uc2 * Does not expect major capital outflows in banking sector\par \par \uc2 * Doesn't expect near-term mergers in sector either\par \par \uc2 By Karolina Slowikowska and Pawel Florkiewicz\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, July 9 (Reuters) - Poland does not expect the zloty to exhibit high volatility, a deputy governor of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said, playing down chances of a repeat of last year's heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  that ate into the bank's hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with Reuters, Witold Kozinski said western Europe looked to be moving closer to solving its debt problems, welcoming a deal at last month's EU summit to leverage the region's rescue funds to better support struggling states' finances..\par \par \uc2 He said the agreement meant less market turmoil for Poland, whose assets were additionally underpinned by the government's efforts to cut the public deficit and healthy, albeit slowing growth rates.\par \par \uc2 "Poland's economic outlook is very positive in my opinion. It is no wonder then that the zloty is faring well," Kozinski, responsible for market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said.\par \par \uc2 The bank, which acts to reduce zloty volatility rather than target a specific exchange level, last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in December, but dealers remain on alert for further \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy was the only one in the European Union not to tip into recession since 2008, but weakness in the euro zone - to which Poland is heavily exposed - drove strong volatility in the zloty last year, when it fluctuated between 3.9 and 4.6 against the euro.\par \par \uc2 Since the start of 2012, the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gained 5.5 percent and held in a much more stable trading pattern.\par \par \uc2 "I believe (volatility) .. will not be a big (this year)," Kozinski, who does not sit on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ratesetting panel, Kozinski added in comments cleared for publication on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "Since the zloty is the most liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region, it is more prone to volatility. But it is not the kind of volatility that would worry us, at least for now."\par \par \uc2 "...The euro zone did not fall apart. Greece is rebuilding itself after its election...the euro zone is consolidating... All this together has, of course, an impact on the zloty's stability."\par \par \uc2 BANKING BUFFER?\par \par \uc2 Kozinski, who also oversees the banking sector as a member of Poland's banking supervisory body, downplayed the risk of banking troubles in the euro zone leading to significant capital outflows from Poland.\par \par \uc2 Some two-thirds of the Polish banking sector is in foreign hands and many of the parent banks have been squeezed for cash, raising fears that their Polish affiliates may have to reduce their lending capacity, undermining the country's growth.\par \par \uc2 The European Bank for Reconstruction and Development (EBRD), set up in 1991 to manage the transition of former communist countries to market economies, recently warned that a new banking crunch in the euro zone risks prompting sharp a retreat by western parent banks.\par \par \uc2 "We do not see capital outflows from Polish banks that are foreign-owned. There is no so-called deleveraging, no loan withdrawals or sucking deposits out of the sector," Kozinski said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also ready to respond with funding in case a troubled parent bank was forced to sell its local business.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be willing to participate in such an undertaking," which would not mean taking the lender over, he said.\par \par \uc2 "(But) I do not expect any mergers in the commercial banking sector any time soon."\par \par \uc2 Kozinski cast doubt on Poland's approval of a European Union's drive to create a regionwide banking union.\par \par \uc2 "We've always had the view that national banking supervisory bodies should not be stripped of any of their current competencies."\par \par \uc2 (Editing by John Stonestreet)\par \par \uc2 POLAND-ZLOTY/ (INTERVIEW) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | PX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120712e879000ww\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
