\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Weak Zloty Won't Push Poland's Debt Above Limit - BGK\b0\par\par\uc2 649 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2012\par 14:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 31 May 2012 08:43 EDT *DJ  BGK Deputy Chief Kowalczyk: Ready To Take Unorthodox PLN Measures\par \par \uc2 31 May 2012 08:43 EDT *DJ  BGK Kowalczyk: EUR/PLN Fair Value Is Around 4.0\par \par \uc2 31 May 2012 08:43 EDT DJ  INTERVIEW: Weak Zloty Won't Push Poland's Debt Above Limit - BGK\par \par \uc2 By Patryk Wasilewski\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 WARSAW (Dow Jones)--Poland's public debt won't breach the country's self-imposed safety thresholds this year despite the zloty's recent and potential future weakening because of government steps to reduce the public debt and deficit, the deputy head of state-owned BGK bank Wojciech Kowalczyk told Dow Jones Newswires.\par \par \uc2 The bank acts as the Polish finance ministry's agent in the zloty market, where it has been present since last year selling foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the zloty. It was particularly active at the end of last year to prop up the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A weak zloty inflates the value of Polish public debt that's denominated in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , boosting overall public debt, which was near 55% of economic output at the end of last year. Foreign debt makes up some 30% of Poland's total.\par \par \uc2 The breach of the 55% threshold would trigger austerity measures aimed at balancing the budget.\par \par \uc2 Calculated in line with local methodology, which excludes some debt categories from the tally, Poland's public debt was at 53.5% of gross domestic product last year. Poland expects debt to fall to 50.5% of GDP in 2012.\par \par \uc2 BGK's Kowalczyk said the bank and the finance ministry are closely watching the market and are ready to step in to "take unorthodox measures" if the ministry deems it necessary.\par \par \uc2 "This year Poland is reducing its debt. Deficit will fall below 3% and debt to 50.5%, and thus the zloty is not a threat to debt," Kowalczyk said.\par \par \uc2 "Moreover, the zloty's weakening is not justified by [Poland's] fundamentals. Investors are taking into account both of these facts in their strategies for the zloty," he added.\par \par \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied in first four months of this year against the euro, temporarily going below PLN4.1 to the euro, but rising worries about the euro zone's future and risk aversion sent the zloty back to around PLN4.4 to the euro as of Thursday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from both the ministry and \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials, as well as BGK's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling reported by traders, have helped moderate losses in the zloty amid the euro's fall against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The BGK deputy chief also said Poland's economic fundamentals are strong and the zloty is undervalued as a result of negative global sentiment because of the situation in Greece. The zloty's fair value is around PLN4.0 against the euro, he said.\par \par \uc2 "Our strong fundamentals can be seen in prices of [Poland's] 10-year paper... If Poland was weak fundamentally, we would be seeing outflows, not inflows by international investors," Kowalczyk said.\par \par \uc2 The yield on Polish 10-year government bonds was at 5.46% Thursday, below 5.82% for Italian paper and 6.51% for Spanish paper.\par \par \uc2 After the verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which signaled the readiness of the government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to act, the zloty's stabilized temporarily but some market participants questioned whether the ministry and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have enough firepower to support it in the longer term.\par \par \uc2 The BGK deputy chief noted Poland has $30 billion available in a flexible credit line from the International Monetary Fund, and that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of $88 billion provide an additional safety cushion.\par \par \uc2 -By Patryk Wasilewski, Dow Jones Newswires; +48 22 447 2430; patryk.wasilewski@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 31, 2012 08:43 ET (12:43 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120531e85v004fj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
