\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Says Ready For Zloty  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 480 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2012\par 17:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 -- Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official reiterates \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  warning if zloty weakens further\par \par \uc2 -- Finance minister "not surprised" by zloty's recent weakening\par \par \uc2 -- Market thinks \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will stay out unless the zloty weakens much more\par \par \uc2 (Adds detail, comment.)\par \par \uc2 By Marcin Sobczyk and Patryk Wasilewski\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 RADOM, Poland (Dow Jones)--The National Bank of Poland is able to step into the zloty market at any time, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said Thursday, but market participants doubt the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is weak enough for the bank to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We have high foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and we're always able to counteract any significant weakening and volatility in the zloty," Witold Kozinski, a member of the bank's executive board, told reporters Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The zloty has been under pressure since Greek political leaders failed to form a coalition government in the wake of inconclusive elections earlier this month. The Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at around EUR4.37 Thursday, nearly 4% lower than in early May.\par \par \uc2 The Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times in the second half of last year, with the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September when the zloty was above EUR4.50 and weakening rapidly. Within minutes, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the exchange rate well below EUR4.40, with its governor saying the bank saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a warning to market participants not to bet against the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Polish monetary authorities have in recent days repeatedly warned that they could re-enter the market at any time. But the finance ministry, which Wednesday returned to selling its euros in the spot market, said the zloty is stronger and less volatile now than when the ministry and the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year.\par \par \uc2 "I'm not surprised that the zloty is reacting this way," Finance Minister Jan Vincent-Rostowski said Thursday. "It always does when the euro weakens," he said, adding that the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is stronger than at the end of 2011, even though the euro is at a roughly similar level to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Market participants believe the current level of the zloty doesn't warrant an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's point of view.\par \par \uc2 "We believe further weakening is possible and the policy of NBP \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far suggests the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't play against the trend. If the zloty depreciates tracking the global sentiment, the NBP will stay out of the market," analysts at BRE said.\par \par \uc2 "Poland won't act on the zloty yet," said \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 , adding that the likelihood of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will only increase when the zloty reaches EUR4.50, the level at which \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  started last year.\par \par \uc2 -By Patryk Wasilewski and Marcin Sobczyk, Dow Jones Newswires, +48 22 447 2432;\par \par \uc2 marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 17, 2012 11:56 ET (15:56 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120517e85h005oh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
