\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 , Debt Slip In Anxious Markets\b0\par\par\uc2 584 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2012\par 22:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  see more modest losses\par \par \uc2 --Emerging market debt weakens slightly\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Central-bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  becoming more frequent\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Erin McCarthy \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The downward slide in emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and debt seen this week slowed slightly Thursday, though these assets were still under pressure in anxious markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ongoing concerns about Europe's sovereign-debt crisis and political uncertainty in debt-laden Greece put broader markets on edge this week, hitting higher-yielding assets, like emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and bonds, especially hard. Fears that Greece could exit the euro zone have escalated, with Fitch Ratings downgrading its ratings on Greece two notches further into junk territory and pointing to increased risk that Greece may exit the monetary union.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, disappointing U.S. economic data Thursday reminded investors of the potential for a sluggish U.S. and global recovery. The Philadelphia Fed said its index of general business activity within the factory sector fell to -5.8 in May from 8.5 in April, marking the first negative reading in eight months.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Everyday it seems like it's either [the] U.S. slowdown, euro-zone debt crisis or China" worrying markets, said Win Thin, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brown Brothers Harriman\f28 \uc2 \f2 's global head of emerging market strategy. "I don't think anyone's going to go long risk right now, given the uncertainty."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The risk premium on emerging market sovereign debt, as seen on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  Emerging Markets Bond Index Global, or Embig, widened by four basis points to 399 basis points over Treasurys. In price terms, the index fell 0.3%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Among \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the Mexican peso underperformed, falling 0.3% against the dollar, which bought MXN13.8142, according to CQG. The Mexican peso often tracks broader markets, as it is one of the more easily and widely traded emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . In addition, it typically underperforms when U.S. data disappoints, given the close economic ties between Mexico and its northern neighbor.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elsewhere in the region, the Chilean peso fell heavily, on the back of deteriorating international copper prices. As Chile is the world's largest producer of the metal, the peso often tracks copper prices. The Chilean peso dived to its weakest level against the dollar in four months. The dollar traded above the key CLP505 level, to buy CLP505.50 late Thursday, according to CQG.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  saw more modest losses than in previous sessions. The Hungarian forint slipped 0.4% against the euro, which changed hands at HUF297.88 from HUF296.63 late Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Polish zloty traded flat on the day against the euro, which changed hands at PLN4.3570. Investors are on guard for further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to shore up the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from Polish authorities. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Finance Ministry has already sold foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the zloty this week, while Poland's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday it is ready to step into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if necessary.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to protect flagging emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has become a recurring theme. India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been noted to be frequently \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets lately, and was suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Thursday. Still, the Indian rupee slid to an all-time low against the dollar Thursday. Later in the session, the dollar was up 0.2% at INR54.41, according to CQG.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Erin McCarthy, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2712; erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com @djfxtrader [ 17-05-12 2005GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120517e85h0010a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
