\par\par \b \uc2 NBP Belka: Polish Zloty Stable Versus Euro In Long Term\b0\par\par\uc2 193 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 10:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is glad to have a floating zloty, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's high volatility is a nuisance, which the bank managed to reduce through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year, National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Marek Belka said Friday.\par \par \uc2 "We are happy with the floating exchange rate because in our view it prevents Poland from being overflown with foreign capital," he told a conference in Prague. "Too much of foreign capital is quite dangerous and this additional risk that comes from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility moderates inflows of foreign capital."\par \par \uc2 "On the other hand, when you look at inflation--our main mandate--this obviously is a nuisance and not incidentally we decided to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to be present in the market, in the last few months to somehow limit the volatility of the zloty. We think we've managed to reduce zloty volatility," he added.\par \par \uc2 Belka added that the zloty remains stable in nominal terms to the euro in the longer term.\par \par \uc2 -By Marcin Sobczyk, Dow Jones Newswires, +48 22 447 2432;\par \par \uc2 marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com [ 16-03-12 0959GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120316e83g000l4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
