\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MONEY-Polish govt, c.bank fall out over  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Chris Borowski and Dagmara Leszkowicz   \par \uc2 909 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2012\par 11:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Jan 26 (Reuters) - The honeymoon is over in the unusual marriage between Poland's government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in supporting the zloty, with barbs flying over the bank's independence.\par \par \uc2 If the two sides don't patch things up, the most liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bond market in the European Union's eastern wing may suffer as policy transparency suffers and foreign investors eye the exits in markets exposed to the euro zone crisis or debt-laden Hungary.\par \par \uc2 After nearly a year of cooperating to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Finance Minister Jacek Rostowski appeared to overstep the mark in early January, calling on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the bond market in the event of panic selling or a "foreign virus".\par \par \uc2 The comments from the British-born former academic raised hackles at the independent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though they were still a far cry from Hungarian Prime Minister Viktor Orban's open moves to tighten his grip on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Budapest.\par \par \uc2 "It looks like something has cracked between the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Finance Ministry," said Piotr Kalisz, chief economist at \uc2 Citibank Handlowy\uc2  in Warsaw.\par \par \uc2 "So far we've had smooth cooperation, and this could be the first sign of a small conflict. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  simply wants to show its independence. They don't want to be seen as the arm of the Finance Ministry."\par \par \uc2 But Rostowski, who in the past spoke with reverence of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's independence, then raised even more eyebrows by saying that the dogma of an independent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is out of whack with its original purpose as a state lender.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's response was swift and unequivocal.\par \par \uc2 It shot back within hours that it "may not substitute the government in its functions, especially with respect to public debt management" - a ringing slap compared with the usually dull rhetoric of economic policy.\par \par \uc2 Rate-setters made their point again after their monthly meeting two weeks later, saying the bank's guidelines "do not allow for the possibility of the NBP (National Bank of Poland) purchasing Treasury securities as a monetary policy instrument".\par \par \uc2 Thu Lan Nguyen, an economist at \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  in Frankfurt, praised the bank for defending its independence.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to make its stance clear, so the government doesn't rely on them and people do indeed expect them to take actions if we would see such a scenario of rising bond yields," he said.\par \par \uc2 "It is the purpose of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be independent, and the NBP has made that clear."\par \par \uc2 In any case, the institutional tag-team was a rare departure from the typical model in emerging Europe, where burgeoning economies have fought to shrug off their centrally planned communist past to build the type of credibility seen elsewhere in the EU, where rules shield central banks from government meddling.\par \par \uc2 Still, that model has suffered erosion over the past year.\par \par \uc2 Hungary has drawn fire - and the threat of court action - from the European Commission, which has accused Orban's government of undermining the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's independence with a series of new laws.\par \par \uc2 And even as many politicians criticise Budapest, some of the same officials are encouraging the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy up bonds of troubled euro zone economies, a move that does not sit well with more conservative policy chiefs.\par \par \uc2 TRANSPARENCY\par \par \uc2 In Poland, the government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have a vested interest in protecting the zloty, which shed as much as 17 percent from peak to trough last year.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market several times since September to help prevent inflation from seeping in from abroad via imported energy and commodity prices.\par \par \uc2 The Finance Ministry, which agreed with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to convert EU funds on the open market through state-owned BGK bank in April, wants a stronger zloty to keep down the value of the one-third of Poland's borrowings denominated in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , keeping state debt below a key constitutional level.\par \par \uc2 BGK's role as the ministry's market arm has been growing, assuming a function similar to what Rostowski had suggested for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  by defending the zloty and bonds.\par \par \uc2 Market players widely expect BGK to cast a constant shadow in the spot market and keep potential sellers guessing, diving in even more at the end of the year, as it did in the last two, to protect the government's year-end debt calculations.\par \par \uc2 But BGK has less than a tenth of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves, making it more vulnerable to a sustained attack.\par \par \uc2 "We expect BGK to be some kind of a moderator on the spot market throughout the year. The question is: to what extent can it play that role?" one Warsaw-based dealer said.\par \par \uc2 BGK's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  pose other problems, too.\par \par \uc2 It is normally the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's duty to protect the zloty with its 76 billion euros of reserves and its mandate to keep prices stable, so an \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  finance ministry clouds the policy environment.\par \par \uc2 "The issue with involving a more directly politically controlled institution and an institution with a leveraged balance sheet is that this transparency, accountability and predictability are muddied," said Peter Attard Montalto, economist at Nomura.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  backstop is more transparent and more accountable."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 POLAND\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (CEE MONEY)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120130e81r000qx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
