\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED-POLL-Polish rate cut seen delayed to Q3 on zloty risks\b0\par\par\uc2 705 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2012\par 16:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Corrects in 2nd paragraph to median expectation instead of all analysts)\par \par \uc2 * All 24 analysts polled see unchanged rates at Jan 10-11 meeting\par \par \uc2 * Median shows first cut postponed until Q3 2012, from Q2 last month\par \par \uc2 * Analysts say risk of weaker zloty feeding into CPI will prevent cuts\par \par \uc2 By Marcin Goettig\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Jan 3 (Reuters) - Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will probably cut interest rates in the third quarter, later than previously expected due to concerns that a weaker zloty might further fuel inflation, a Reuters poll showed on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The median expectation of 24 analysts polled by Reuters between December 23 and January 3 sees the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Council cutting the key interest rate by 25 basis points in the third quarter and by another 25 basis points in the fourth.\par \par \uc2 Last month analysts also expected a total of 50 basis points in rates cuts this year but saw the first cut coming in the second quarter.\par \par \uc2 All of the 24 analysts polled predict the MPC will hold fire at its January 10-11 rate meeting.\par \par \uc2 "With the persisting depreciation pressure on the zloty, elevated level of current CPI and still strong economic activity indicators, the MPC will keep rates on hold and maintain the hawkish rhetoric in order to safeguard the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Piotr Bujak of \uc2 Nordea Bank Polska\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the main interest rate\par \par \uc2 by a total of 100 basis points in the first half of last year, bringing it to 4.50 percent by June. It has adopted a wait-and-see approach since then.\par \par \uc2 The bank last cut interest rates in June 2009 to help the economy fight the spreading global economic crisis.\par \par \uc2 The zloty has lost around 11 percent against the euro since August 2011 on fears that the euro zone debt crisis might spiral out of control, causing a retreat of investors from emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 The weakening domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed inflation higher through higher prices of imported goods, exacerbating a global rise in energy and food prices.\par \par \uc2 Price growth is expected to stand at an annual 4.6 percent year-on-year in December, remaining significantly above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 2.5 percent target.\par \par \uc2 But the slide of the zloty also helped the economy to beat forecasts in the third quarter of 2011 and post growth of more than 4 percent year-on-year.\par \par \uc2 Zloty depreciation, coupled with a large internal market of 38 million consumers, helped Poland avoid recession after the collapse of \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Poland's growth is now set to slow again to around 3 percent in 2012, with the government's fiscal consolidation plan additionally weighing on economic activity.\par \par \uc2 "I do not think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may afford to cut rates soon as it will weaken the zloty that will feed into higher inflation," said Guillaume Tresca, emerging market strategist at \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2 , adding the situation in the euro zone should stabilise by summer.\par \par \uc2 Forward rate agreements currently price in the first 25 basis point rate cut in July.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  six times on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since the start of September to defend the weakening zloty and any cut in interest rates could hurt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  more due to a lower risk premium of investing in Polish bonds.\par \par \uc2 "Inflation will decelerate rather slowly, remaining above 4 percent in the first quarter due to the earlier zloty depreciation and, among others, a rise of the diesel excise tax," said Dariusz Winek, chief economist at Bank BGZ.\par \par \uc2 "In the coming weeks one should expect more zloty weakness so it is hard to speak of a fast start of rate cuts," Winek added.\par \par \uc2 Polish state bank BGK intensified its euro sales from European Union structural funds ahead of the year-end \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixing that is used to calculate Polish state debt.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts expect that its reduced presence on the market at the beginning of the year might leave the zloty more exposed to global risk aversion and a possible further deterioration of the situation in Hungary.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Marcin Goettig; editing by Anna Willard)\par \par \uc2 POLAND-RATES/ (POLL) (CORRECTED)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120106e813000xu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
