\par\par \b \uc2 Polish  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2 : No Legal Objections To Buying Bonds\b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Januar 2012\par 16:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the bond market only if a "deep" crisis threatened the stability of the country's financial system, the bank said Monday, admitting the constitution doesn't forbid such a move.\par \par \uc2 However, the bank added, Poland's bond prices and financial system remain stable and its banks don't require a significant increase in capital, suggesting there are no grounds for such an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the moment.\par \par \uc2 "This means purchase of bonds on the secondary market by the [National Bank of Poland] could take place only in situations of deep crisis, when stability of the financial system is threatened," the bank wrote, adding the Polish banking and financial system remains sound at the moment.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  added that its monetary policy council didn't include bond market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as one of potential policy instruments in monetary policy guidelines for 2012.\par \par \uc2 Poland's finance ministry and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  were active on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last year to defend the zloty from excessive weakening and earlier on Monday, Finance Minister Jan Vincent Rostowski said the bank could step into the bond market in case of panic or contagion from abroad.\par \par \uc2 The bank warned speculation about a significant drop in bond prices or a need for its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market "could lead to unwanted perception of such information by financial markets," and could prove a self-fulfilling prophecy by affecting bond and zloty prices.\par \par \uc2 -By Patryk Wasilewski, Dow Jones Newswires; +48 22 447 2430; patryk.wasilewski@dowjones.com [ 02-01-12 1609GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120102e8120009y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
