\par\par \b \uc2 2nd UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Poland Intervenes \highlight\uc2  To Strengthen Zloty\b0\par\par\uc2 348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 2011\par 18:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it bought zlotys Thursday\par \par \uc2 --Dealers said the finance ministry also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market\par \par \uc2 --The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed EUR/PLN to around 4.41 from 4.46\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Patryk Wasilewski \par    Of \f28 \uc2 \f2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Adds \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  confirmation, details on BGK)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WARSAW (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 )--\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and finance ministry \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Thursday to shore up the zloty, just ahead of the last trading day of the year when the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's fixing is traditionally used to value the country's foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  debt pile.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , NBP, stepped in to buy the zloty after the Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened significantly Thursday to 4.462 against the euro. The move quickly pushed it to around 4.41.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Today in the afternoon NBP sold some foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in exchange for the zloty," the bank said in a statement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dealers said state-owned bank BGK, which acts as the finance ministry's agent in the market, was also selling euros Thursday, supporting the zloty's strengthening.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The finance ministry uses the zloty's last fixing of the year to determine the size of the country's foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  debt; a stronger zloty reduces the country's debt ratios. Around a third of Poland's debt is foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -denominated.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Deputy Finance Minister Dominik Radziwill said earlier this month that the ministry would be selling on the market "significant amounts" of euros it has available from the European Union's funds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NBP has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market several times this year when it has considered market behaviour "disorderly," usually meaning the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was depreciating at a pace the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  deemed too fast.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials have often said the bank doesn't have a target level for the zloty, but it won't shy away from taking action to curb volatility or excessive weakening.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 16:50 GMT EUR/PLN trades at 4.405.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Patryk Wasilewski, Dow Jones Newswires; +48 22 447 2430; patryk.wasilewski@dowjones.com [ 29-12-11 1702GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111229e7ct000li\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
