\par\par \b \uc2 CHARTING MARKETS: Polish  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Weakens Support\b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 2011\par 23:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --The Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought the zloty earlier Thursday\par \par \uc2 --Now a euro move below PLZ4.3791 would point to PLZ4.2477\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Stephen Cox, CMT \par    A \f28 \uc2 \f2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\f28 \uc2 \f2  COLUMN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and finance ministry to strengthen the zloty Thursday appears to have been well timed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It very well may have weakened the EUR/PLZ pair by pulling technical support out from the euro.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pushed EUR/PLZ to around 4.41 from 4.46 earlier Thursday, observers noted. The Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dipped into its stock of euros to buy zlotys after its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened significantly against the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday, when the euro reached PLZ4.462.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But well before Thursday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  it was clear on the daily chart that a technical breakdown of the euro might be complete.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In fact the euro broke down on the daily chart on Dec. 16 when it took out trend channel support at PLZ4.5037. That move by itself pointed the euro to the PLZ4.3881-PLZ4.3633 support band. Sure enough, the euro's lowest reading since the technical breakdown is Wednesday's low, PLZ4.3791.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Now PLZ4.3791 may be the last euro support in the way of an eventual test of PLZ4.2477.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It's apparent in any case that the euro has been compromised for now. Earlier the euro recorded a strong intraday high, PLZ4.4660. Current trading is PLZ4.4119. The current intraday low is now PLZ4.3861.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Stephen Cox, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; 212-416-2212; stephen.cox@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Stephen Cox, a chartered market technician, is chief technician for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \uc2 \f2 .)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Data by CQG)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAmericas@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments.) [ 12-29-11 1722ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1081 4247   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020111229e7ct00049\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
