\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Polish  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Chief: PLN Volatility Helps Stabilize Economy\b0\par\par\uc2 624 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Dezember 2011\par 10:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 21 Dec 2011 04:25 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: EUR/PLN In 2001, Early 2011 Roughly Unchanged\par \par \uc2 21 Dec 2011 04:27 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: Zloty More Exposed To Speculation Due To Liquid Market\par \par \uc2 21 Dec 2011 04:29 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: EUR/PLN At 4.44, Wouldn't Like EUR/PLN Around 3.44\par \par \uc2 21 Dec 2011 04:29 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: Potential Zloty \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Plays Moderating Role\par \par \uc2 21 Dec 2011 04:29 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: Not True NBP Spent EUR5B, Much Less Spent On \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 21 Dec 2011 04:30 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: Notes Reports EUR1B Spent Sep-Oct On PLN \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 21 Dec 2011 04:30 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  Are Part Of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy\par \par \uc2 21 Dec 2011 04:30 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: Poland \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Has No Zloty Target Level\par \par \uc2 21 Dec 2011 04:31 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: Weaker Zloty Stokes Inflationary Pressure\par \par \uc2 21 Dec 2011 04:32 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: PLN \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Boosted \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Profit By PLN700M\par \par \uc2 21 Dec 2011 04:32 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  Can Afford \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  In Zloty Market\par \par \uc2 21 Dec 2011 04:33 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: Zloty Has Potential To Strengthen\par \par \uc2 21 Dec 2011 04:35 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: Polish Constitution Doesn't Ban Financing Other States' Debt\par \par \uc2 21 Dec 2011 04:37 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: No Stock Market Bubbles In Poland\par \par \uc2 21 Dec 2011 04:39 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: Stock Market Is A Casino, Don't Overestimate Analysis\par \par \uc2 21 Dec 2011 04:44 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: Reiterates Support For Ownership Changes In Banking System\par \par \uc2 21 Dec 2011 04:46 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: Doesn't Recommend Rush For Poland To Adopt Euro\par \par \uc2 21 Dec 2011 06:30 EDT DJ  Polish Zloty \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  Soothe Market, May Have Cost EUR1B\par \par \uc2 WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the zloty market have limited the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's short-term volatility, said Marek Belka, governor of the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times since September to prop up the zloty, weakened by the euro-zone's debt crisis. At 1110 GMT Wednesday, the zloty was around PLN4.43 to the euro, some 11% weaker than in August.\par \par \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent "a much smaller amount" then EUR5 billion on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Belka told a parliamentary committee Wednesday, acknowledging local reports of EUR1 billion spent on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September and October. With reserve assets above EUR70 billion, \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  can afford to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, he said.\par \par \uc2 Belka reiterated the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no exchange rate target for the zloty and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to counter speculative moves. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is more exposed to speculation than regional peers, like the Czech koruna or the Hungarian forint, because of the much larger depth of the Polish financial market. The value of Polish assets are similar to Brazil's, while the Polish economy is several times smaller, Belka said.\par \par \uc2 "When people want to speculate, they will speculate with the zloty. With the Czech koruna, there's no money to be made because there are no Czech assets," Belka said.\par \par \uc2 In the longer term, the zloty is very stable, Belka added, noting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was around PLN4 to the euro in 2001 and again ten years later in early 2011. Short-term volatility helps stabilize the Polish economy, with consumers switching to domestic production when the zloty weakens which makes imported products more expensive, he said.\par \par \uc2 -By Marcin Sobczyk, Dow Jones Newswires; +48 22 447 2432; marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 21, 2011 06:30 ET (11:30 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020111221e7cl0024f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
