\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Polish cbank head: zloty has potential to appreciate\b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Dezember 2011\par 10:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (combines takes, adds background)\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Dec 21 (Reuters) - The Polish zloty has stabilised due to the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has potential to appreciate in value, the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The zloty has lost as much as 12 percent versus the euro since August as investors fled riskier assets due to the euro zone crisis but has regained some ground since last week on expectations of ramped up euro sales by Poland's state bank BGK.\par \par \uc2 "If we observe the situation in the last few months when the zloty depreciated from fundamental levels then there exists the potential for appreciation," Marek Belka told a parliamentary hearing.\par \par \uc2 The zloty traded up 0.3 percent to the euro from Tuesday's close at 4.437 at 1022 GMT, rising for the sixth consecutive session.\par \par \uc2 Polish authorities have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the zloty four times since September and many observers assume the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the finance ministry -- through BGK -- will remain active to prevent the breaching of a key debt ceiling at the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 A third of Polish state debt is denominated in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and so it is vulnerable to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swings.\par \par \uc2 Belka said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had spent "several times less than 5 billion euros" in its recent market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the zloty.\par \par \uc2 The governor also told lawmakers \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  would lend 6.26 to 6.27 billion euros in additional funds to the International Monetary Fund under a plan to raise the fund's crisis-fighting capability so it can help indebted euro zone states.\par \par \uc2 His comments echoed an earlier statement by Finance Minister Jacek Rostowski.\par \par \uc2 Poland, the largest eastern European Union economy, is not a member of the euro.\par \par \uc2 EU leaders agreed earlier this month to offer 200 billion euros in bilateral loans to the IMF as part of moves to stem the euro zone debt crisis that also included a move to deeper fiscal integration within the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bloc.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Karolina Slowikowska and Pawel Sobczak)\par \par \uc2 POLAND-BELKA/  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111224e7cl0007p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
