\par\par \b \uc2 REFILE-CEE MONEY-PLN  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  made less likely by market moves\b0\par\par\uc2 707 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 2011\par 15:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Removes extra headline at top of text)\par \par \uc2 * Polish authorities may not need to step into \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market\par \par \uc2 * Fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  prompts investors to close long EURPLN\par \par \uc2 * Warsaw improves its debt through bills buyback, selling debt to local govt\par \par \uc2 By Dagmara Leszkowicz\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Dec 20 (Reuters) - The fear among traders of being on the wrong side of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the thinning pre-holiday market means authorities may achieve their goal of keeping the zloty relatively strong this month without having to act.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the zloty four times since September and many observers had assumed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the finance ministry -- through a state-owned BGK bank -- would remain active to prevent breaching a key debt ceiling at the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 A third of the state debt is denominated in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and so it is susceptible to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swings.\par \par \uc2 But the jumpy foreign players, which helped chop a tenth off the zlotys' value since August, have instead given the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a short term boost in recent days.\par \par \uc2 "Those big names who have recently bet on the zloty fall, apparently started to buy the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Karol Zaluski, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at \uc2 ING Bank Slaski\uc2 . "It looks like either the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or the BGK \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't be necessary, at least for now."\par \par \uc2 Another trader said, "Investors probably felt that there is no use to collide with BGK and to post losses."\par \par \uc2 Yet, there are other reasons why the zloty has come off its recent lows of 4.6 to the euro set earlier this month and now trades closer to 4.46.\par \par \uc2 Under Polish law, if public debt breaches 55 percent of gross domestic product (GDP), the government is required to make painful spending cuts.\par \par \uc2 The public debt is expected to stand at 53.8 pct of GDP and analysts see the 55 percent threshold being breached only if the zloty weakens past 4.7-4.8 to the euro.\par \par \uc2 OTHER WAYS\par \par \uc2 Concerned that the gathering clouds of the euro zone could cast a shadow over the zloty, the finance ministry has moved to reduce the debt on its own books by shifting a part of it to local governments.\par \par \uc2 "Buying of the treasury papers by local governments will lower public debt by their nominal value," said Piotr Marczak, the head of the Finance Ministry's debt department.\par \par \uc2 So far only Warsaw confirmed it could buy the government's papers for up to 550 million zloty. But the proposal has been put forward also to other local governments.\par \par \uc2 "Information about a possibility of putting money in treasury's papers was sent to those local governments that reported a solid amount of free cash at the end of the second quarter," said a deputy head of the ministry's debt department, Bogdan Klimaszewski.\par \par \uc2 To trim state debt, the ministry also bought back a total of 4.2 billion zlotys in treasury bills this year, with the last buy-back tender held on Monday. The recent tender lowered this year's ratio of debt to Gross Domestic Product by around 0.15 percent.\par \par \uc2 "After the Monday buyback, we estimate that the debt/GDP ratio stands at 54.1 percent," said Marcin Mazurek, senior analyst at BRE bank in Warsaw.\par \par \uc2 Some economists say that Finance Minister Jacek Rostowski is determined to improve the country's indicators in terms of debt and deficit as he sees a real chance of a ratings upgrade.\par \par \uc2 Two rating agencies -- \uc2 Moody's\uc2  and \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  -- have recently pointed to Poland's fiscal situation as key to the country's rating.\par \par \uc2 Moody's\uc2  confirmed the country's rating on Tuesday and said the outlook was stable due to Warsaw's fiscal strategy and a strong track in the face of significant external shocks.\par \par \uc2 S&P also said that deep, long-term structural reforms would put Poland in a good position to unlock its growth potential.\par \par \uc2 Moody's\uc2  rates Poland at A2, while S&P and Fitch rates it at A-, all with a stable outlook.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Dagmara Leszkowicz; editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 POLAND-ZLOTY/(ANALYSIS)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111223e7ck000th\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
