\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MORNING BRIEFING:  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Weakness Fueling Inflation\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sean Carney, Marynia Kruk & Veronika Gulyas   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 959 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Dezember 2011\par 05:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    TODAY'S CALENDAR \par  \par    Local/GMT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0900/0800 Hungary November inflation\f28 \par \par \uc2 1000/0900 Czech current account balance for October\par \par \uc2 1130/1030 Hungary 3-month treasury bill auction\par \par \uc2 1400/1300 Poland's statistics office releases November CPI data\par \par \uc2 Consumer price pressures are rising throughout the region while economic activity and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  values fall, raising concerns over a possible bout of stagflation on the European Union's eastern flank.\par \par \uc2 In Poland, November inflation is expected to spike to 4.5% from 4.3% in October, while in Hungary inflation is seen rising to 4.3% on the year in November from 3.9% the month before.\par \par \uc2 The upcoming readings are set to follow a spike in inflation announced late last week, in which the consumer price index accelerated to 2.5% on the year in November, above market expectations of 2.4% and above a 2.3% rate in October.\par \par \uc2 Piotr Bujak, an economist at \uc2 Nordea Bank\uc2  in Warsaw, said one of the culprits behind the spike in consumer prices is weakness among regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the last few months due to risk aversion amid the euro-zone crisis.\par \par \uc2 "This will fuel inflation, especially of food and fuels, as well as other imported products," Bujak said.\par \par \uc2 Unlike in neighboring countries, Polish consumer demand remained resilient in November, as Poles continued shopping.\par \par \uc2 In Hungary, analysts are attributing the spike to a recent excise tax hike, but the heavy forint depreciation may also become more visible in the figures, they said.\par \par \uc2 Erste Bank expects to see a jump again in January, when the value-added tax will rise to 27% from 25%.\par \par \uc2 This will likely push the annual figure well above 5% in the first few months of next year and then inflation should slow to 4% by year-end as consumer demand is weak.\par \par \uc2 Erste said it expects the Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lift interest rates by 50 basis points to 7% this month, and that this tightening will allow rates to be stable next year.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par         Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par         0350 GMT   2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par EUR/CZK 25.688-744 25.672-748 +0.02 25.709   25.722  +2.65 \par EUR/HUF 306.05-74 305.76-07  +0.02   306.27   306.58 +10.11 \par EUR/PLN 4.5543-602 4.5514-659 -0.03 4.5575   4.5574 +15.17 \par  \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par        Hungary        Poland            Czech Republic \par        Mon    Fri     Mon     Fri       Mon     Fri \par 3 yrs  8.35%  8.20%   4.88%   4.85%(1)  2.34%   2.35%(2) \par 5 yrs  8.75%  8.60%   5.27%   5.22%     2.77%   2.77% \par 10yrs  8.90%  8.80%   5.94%   5.90%     3.96%   3.96% \par (1) 2Yrs (2) 4Yrs \par  \par  \par STOCKS \par EU Enlarged 15     1,676.04   loss    35.87    dn 2.10% \par WIG 20              2,174.78  loss    52.10    dn  2.34% \par BUX                 17121.96   gain     85.93    up 0.5% \par PX                    860.1    loss     13.2     dn 1.5% \par  \par  \par  \par OTHER NEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: Exiled Belarussian opposition leader Ales Mikhalevich was held in Poland Monday on a warrant from Minsk, but was released after several hours following \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the foreign ministry in Warsaw.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 POLAND\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance ministry, at a switching auction Wednesday, will offer bonds maturing in 2015, 2016, and 2021 in exchange for papers maturing in January, April, and July of 2012, the ministry said in a statement Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: The European Union's total contribution to a bailout fund administered by the International Monetary Fund may be below EUR200 billion if some of the bloc's member states don't provide access to sufficient funding, Poland's Deputy Foreign Minister Mikolaj Dowgielewicz told a press conference Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: Polish power utility \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tauron Polska Energia\f28 \uc2 \f2  SA (TPE.WA) has issued bonds worth 3.3 billion zlotys ($959 million) to finance its acquisition of power distribution company Gornoslaski Zaklad Energetyczny SA from Swedish utility \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vattenfall AB\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the company said in a statement Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CZECH REPUBLIC: The Czechs are likely to contribute money to the International Monetary Fund to be used to support the euro zone, but the amount being requested is very high, the country's finance minister Monday said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It would be unwise to completely refuse" the requested loan for the IMF, nevertheless the amount sought is "extremely high" and it would be more realistic at a lower level, Miroslav Kalousek, Czech minister of finance, said after a press conference.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: Hungary continues to oppose the European Union Core Network Corridor transportation concept, because adding this third level to the Trans-European Transport Network (TEN-T) would entail unwarranted administrative burdens and consume most of the available European Union funding for the initiative, Deputy State Secretary for European Union and International Relations Tamas Ivan Kovacs said in Brussels on Monday, the National Development Ministry reported.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: The Hungarian debt management agency AKK will publish its debt issuance plan next week, after the parliament finalizes the 2012 budget, an agency official told Dow Jones Newswires Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: Visiting Romanian President Traian Basescu said Monday that Romania fully and resolutely supported Turkey's European Union (EU) bid.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: Romania's Prime Minister Emil Boc on Monday called a confidence vote on a new electoral bill fiercely criticized by the opposition.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Sean Carney, Marynia Kruk & Veronika Gulyas, Dow Jones Newswires; +420 222 315 290; sean.carney@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Go to \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe}}}\uc2 \f2  for the new Dow Jones blog on Central and Eastern Europe, covering business, politics, society and more, written by our correspondents across the region. [ 12-12-11 2304ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020111213e7cd0000q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
