\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MORNING BRIEFING: Czech Jobless Rate To Edge Higher\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sean Carney   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 809 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 2011\par 05:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    TODAY'S CALENDAR \par  \par    Local/GMT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0900/0800 Czech jobless rate in November\f28 \par \par \uc2 1000/0900 Czech 3Q current account\par \par \uc2 1000/0900 Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  annual conference\par \par \uc2 1130/1030 Hungary 12-month T-bill tender\par \par \uc2 1400/1300 CFO of Czech utility CEZ holds online interview\par \par \uc2 Fresh Czech unemployment figures due Thursday morning should confirm that the economic slowdown in the euro zone is taking its toll in central Europe, while in Hungary central bankers may comment on the euro zone's rescue plans.\par \par \uc2 In Prague, the jobless rate in November is expected to have edged higher to 8% from 7.9% in October as seasonal jobs came to an end while the country's economic activity cooled.\par \par \uc2 In Budapest, Stefan Ingves, governor of the Swedish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and also head of the Basel Committee on Banking Supervision and the European Systemic Risk Board's expert consult group, will speak at the \uc2 National Bank of Hungary\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Andras Simor and deputy governor Julia Kiraly will likewise speak, while executives from domestic commercial banks are slated to participate.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par         Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par         0350 GMT    2150 GMT         High    Low      12/31 \par EUR/CZK 25.211-59 25.204-70  -0.01   25.233   25.240  +0.73 \par EUR/HUF 300.54-1.24 300.40-1.48 -0.02 300.70 300.88  +8.13 \par EUR/PLN 4.4638-722 4.4588-670 +0.11 4.4660   4.4636 +12.92 \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par        Hungary        Poland            Czech Republic \par        Wed    Tues    Wed     Tues      Wed     Tues \par 3 yrs  8.10%  7.90%   4.82%   4.82%(1)  2.34%   2.35%(2) \par 5 yrs  8.30%  8.25%   5.21%   5.22%     2.77%   2.76% \par 10yrs  8.70%  8.55%   5.89%   5.86%     4.01%   3.95% \par (1) 2Yrs (2) 4Yrs \par  \par  \par STOCKS \par Enlarged EU 15      1,737.64   loss     4.76     dn 0.27% \par WIG20               2,253.57   gain    11.45     up  0.51% \par BUX                 17209.27   loss    163.18    dn  0.9% \par PX                    880.0    loss      9.9     dn  1.1% \par  \par  \par  \par OTHER NEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: Poland's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  plans to continue buying zloty to help the Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weather the euro-zone crisis, its chief said Wednesday. Marek Belka reiterated that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has no particular exchange rate target, describing its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as designed to create a risk for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  speculators.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 POLAND\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : Unemployment in Poland jumped to 12.1 percent in November after holding flat at 11.8 percent from August through to October, the country's labour ministry said Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CZECH REPUBLIC: The Czech Republic finished its 2011 bond-funding program with a disappointing auction which market watchers blamed on the choice of the bond on offer.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Finance Ministry's CZK7 billion ($371.1 million) offer of the October 2023-dated floating rate bond received only CZK5.649 billion in bids and the ministry sold just CZK3.034 billion of the paper.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SLOVAKIA: Slovak lawmakers on Wednesday adopted a 2012 budget with a projected deficit of 4.6% of the gross domestic product (GDP), higher than the originally proposed deficit of 3.8%. "The 4.6% deficit is the maximum level which, with any luck, we won't exceed," Finance Minister Ivan Miklos said after the vote.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: Hungary's year-to-date budget deficit narrowed further in November as the majority of budget revenues are flowing at the end of the year, the national economy ministry said Wednesday. The budget posted a surplus of 79.9 billion forints ($355 million) in November, taking the deficit of the first 11 months to HUF1.15 trillion, or 82% of the full-year deficit target, the ministry said in a statement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: Romania's president Traian Basescu said on Wednesday that his country supports changes in the European Union treaty in order to put an end to the debt crisis in the euro zone.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BULGARIA: European Union nations are unlikely to unanimously agree Friday to a French-German proposal for limited treaty changes to help stem the euro-zone debt crisis, but a deal which would sees the 17 euro-zone countries plus "a few" other EU member states sign up to far-reaching coordination of economic policies, supervision of their budgets through European officials and strict limits on debts and deficits is "likely," Bulgaria's finance minister said Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Sean Carney, Dow Jones Newswires; +420 222 315 290; sean.carney@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Patryk Wasilewski in Warsaw and Gergo Racz in Budapest contributed to this briefing.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Go to \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe}}}\uc2 \f2  for the new Dow Jones blog on Central and Eastern Europe, covering business, politics, society and more, written by our correspondents across the region. [ 12-07-11 2303ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020111208e7c80000t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
