\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  To Continue Zloty  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2011\par 18:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 -- The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  ready to step in if zloty weakens dramatically again\par \par \uc2 -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have proven effective, NBP chief Belka says\par \par \uc2 -- No change of monetary policy view, Polish rates may go either way\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments on the zloty versus regional peers from the fifth paragraph, background on rates in the seventh.)\par \par \uc2 By Marcin Sobczyk\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 WARSAW (Dow Jones)--Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans to continue buying zloty to help the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weather the euro-zone crisis, its chief said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Marek Belka reiterated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no particular exchange rate target, describing its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  as designed to create a risk for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators.\par \par \uc2 "We intend to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in line with rules so far," the governor of the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  told a news conference. "We \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when we recognize signs of destabilization in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market."\par \par \uc2 The bank has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times since September to shore up the zloty, weakened by the euro-zone crisis. The zloty was around PLN4.47 to the euro Wednesday afternoon local time, some 12% weaker than in August.\par \par \uc2 He said the forays have been effective in stabilizing the zloty against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region.\par \par \uc2 "Over the past two months that we've been present in the market, the zloty hasn't weakened anymore and its volatility is lower than of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  we usually compare ourselves with--for example the Hungarian forint and the Czech koruna," he said. "Before our \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the koruna was much more stable than the zloty. Now it's quite the opposite."\par \par \uc2 Earlier, the bank's rate-setting council left its benchmark interest rate unchanged at 4.5%. The Monetary Policy Council acknowledged in a statement that the weak zloty could stoke inflation, which was running at 4.3% on the year in October, above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target of 2.5%.\par \par \uc2 So far this year, the bank has raised rates by one percentage point. The council believes this should bring Poland's inflation back towards target in the mid-term, and slower economic growth and fiscal tightening should also have a moderating effect.\par \par \uc2 -By Marcin Sobczyk, Dow Jones Newswires, +48 22 447 2432;\par \par \uc2 marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 07, 2011 12:11 ET (17:11 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020111207e7c700528\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
