\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Polish State-Owned BGK Props Up Zloty\b0\par\par\uc2 459 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2011\par 19:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Polish state-owned bank BGK seen propping up zloty Wednesday\par \par \uc2 --The action comes a week after \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Clare Connaghan \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--Polish state-owned Bank Gospodarstwa Krajowego was seen buying zloty in "significant amounts" Wednesday, in a move interpreted by traders as an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose sharply in response, pushing the euro down to PLN4.4944 from around PLN4.5370. The dollar fell to a low of PLN3.3344 from PLN3.36. The bank had dipped into the market to sell foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier in the session, but this latest round was much more aggressive.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "(BGK) took an opportunity when the market was in risk-on mood because of the announcement of the swap agreements," said emerging market strategist Thu Lan Nguyen at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sentiment across emerging markets improved markedly after the world's largest central banks took coordinated action to shore up the global financial system, under threat from Europe's rolling debt crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hungarian forint and Czech koruna immediately climbed. But the zloty lagged until BGK jumped into the market for at least the second time Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 All emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have come under heavy selling pressure since the summer when a toxic combination of global economic fears and escalating euro-zone debt worries set off a huge exodus from emerging markets. But Poland's close ties with the troubled euro zone mean the zloty has suffered more than most.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As result, Polish authorities have taken action to stem \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakness, which can pose inflationary problems by lifting the cost of imported goods. For countries burdened with large amounts of debt denominated in foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is particularly harmful because these debts become much more expensive to pay back.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For Poland, that is a particularly sticky issue, as the country has a self-imposed limit on the ratio between debt and gross domestic product. Crossing its 55% limit would trigger an automatic tightening of fiscal policy. The weaker the zloty gets, the closer Poland gets to that limit.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Last week, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was seen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to defend the zloty. BGK, which acts on behalf of Poland's finance ministry, is often active in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. It regularly sells euros it receives as European Union subsidies directly on the market instead of converting them at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 1708 GMT the euro was trading at PLN4.5032 against the Polish zloty, compared with a session high of PLN4.5575.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Clare Connaghan, Dow Jones Newswires; +44 (0) 20 7842 9496, clare.connaghan@dowjones.com @djfxtrader [ 30-11-11 1805GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111130e7bu001a5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
