\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ/Emerging Europe:  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2 's Zloty  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\uc2  Turn Predictable\b0\par\par\uc2 463 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 2011\par 16:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Emerging Europe Real Time is The Wall Street Journal Online's site for news and analysis on Central and Eastern Europe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Posted by Marcin Sobczyk \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  contradicted some of its earlier public declarations when it unsuccessfully \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the depreciating zloty on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  insists it isn't defending any particular exchange rate, yet the four \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far have always occurred when the zloty was in the range of 4.42-4.52 to the euro.\par \par \uc2 Poland's rate-setters also pledged to introduce an element of uncertainty for speculators, yet the timing of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday was painfully predictable.\par \par \uc2 Soon after it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time on Sept. 23, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Marek Belka said the only goal of the move was "to make life more difficult for those who speculate against the zloty."\par \par \uc2 "We're not defending any particular level in the exchange rate. We want to add a risk factor to the game for those who bet the zloty will weaken," he said a day after the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the zloty.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been in free fall despite Poland's comparably healthy growth prospects and resilience to crises as investors fled emerging markets amid the euro-zone debt crisis. As in the post-Lehman crisis of 2008-2009, speculators placed bets the zloty would continue to depreciate.\par \par \uc2 When the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold about EUR1 billion on Sept. 23, it quickly moved the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from 4.52 zlotys to the euro to about 4.38 zlotys, burning those speculators' fingers. Still, despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts, the zloty has fallen about 13% since early August, rendering it one of the worst-performing emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the current crisis. Only the Hungarian forint and the South African rand have done worse.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took the market by surprise. But all of the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  that followed--on Sept. 30, Oct. 3 and Nov. 23--have so far taken place in the range of 4.42-4.52 zlotys to the euro.\par \par \uc2 Market participants go on alert, therefore, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in what's now routinely referred to as "\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  territory," while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's repeated warnings of its readiness to strike has made it quite easy for the markets to guess when the hit is coming.\par \par \uc2 "Usually when the NBP speaks of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it comes soon after," \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  said at 0808 GMT on Wednesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came less than 30 minutes later.\par \par \uc2 -For continuously updated news from The Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 . [ 24-11-11 1551GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111124e7bo000z6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
