\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ/Emerging Europe:  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2 's Latest  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  To Boost Zloty Deemed 'Failure'\b0\par\par\uc2 426 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 2011\par 12:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Emerging Europe Real Time is The Wall Street Journal Online's site for news and analysis on Central and Eastern Europe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Posted by Clare Connaghan \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Blink and you might have missed \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday. The initial leg higher in the zloty has been all but erased now, leaving little trace of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action.\par \par \uc2 Peter Attard Montalto, an emerging-market economist at Nomura in London, calls the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  a "failure" and it certainly looks that way judging by the price action.\par \par \uc2 The zloty was around 4.47 to the euro on Thursday morning, exactly where it was when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold an undisclosed amount of euros in the market Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Up until yesterday, the bank's previous attempts at \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been successful in bringing the zloty down for at least a few days. But Wednesday was no normal day--the tide the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was up against was simply too strong.\par \par \uc2 Germany--long thought of as the safest of euro-zone havens--failed to sell all the bonds it wanted too, cranking up concern about the euro-zone crisis to a new level. The auction result sent shockwaves to investors and emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold off aggressively as a result.\par \par \uc2 No one was immune from the selloff, but \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in central Europe--such as the zloty--with close banking and trade ties with the troubled euro zone, suffered more than most.\par \par \uc2 The question now is what will Polish authorities do. It is clear that Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been ineffective, but that doesn't mean the bank won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness can pose inflationary problems and in countries burdened with debt denominated in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the situation is particularly harmful because these debts become much more expensive to pay back as the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthen.\par \par \uc2 For Poland, that is a particularly thorny issue, as it has a self-imposed limit on the ratio between debt and gross domestic product. Crossing its 55% limit would trigger an automatic tightening of fiscal policy. The weaker the zloty gets, the closer \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  gets to that limit, setting the scene for further \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We will see the NBP back in the market and state-owned Bank Gospodarstwa Krajowego or BGK with more aggression too," says Nomura's Montalto.\par \par \uc2 -For continuously updated news from The Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 . [ 24-11-11 1125GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111124e7bo000r9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
