\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ/Emerging Europe:  \highlight22\uc2 Poland Intervenes \highlight\uc2  Again To Boost Zloty, More Action Likely\b0\par\par\uc2 484 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 2011\par 12:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Emerging Europe Real Time is The Wall Street Journal Online's site for news and analysis on Central and Eastern Europe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope }}}\uc2 ) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Posted by Marcin Sobczyk \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Wednesday to support the zloty, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said. More \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are likely before the year is out.\par \par \uc2 The Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose sharply against the euro and U.S. dollar in response to the suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which pushed the euro down to 4.4423 zlotys from around 4.4792 zlotys. The dollar fell to a low of 3.3995 zlotys from 3.3271 zlotys.\par \par \uc2 Last week, Polish state-owned Bank Gospodarstwa Krajowego--the finance ministry's agent--was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the zloty.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't have a lasting effect, said BGZ, a local bank, as investors move to safer assets ahead of the Thanksgiving holiday in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 According to economists, more \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are likely before the end of the year. The National Bank of Poland and the finance ministry are determined to keep the zloty from spinning out of control, each for different reasons.\par \par \uc2 One of the main reasons behind the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts to boost the zloty is concern that a weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would stoke inflation, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, Marek Belka, said in an interview published Wednesday on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's website. The bank started \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September, when mounting concern over Europe's unresolved sovereign debt problem prompted investors to dump emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  wholesale. Despite Poland's comparatively sound finances and growth prospects, the zloty failed to escape this trend. Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 --if confirmed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 --marks the fourth time that Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to shore up the embattled zloty.\par \par \uc2 In comments for The Wall Street Journal earlier this month, Mr. Belka reiterated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's readiness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any time "to fight disorderly behavior." He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "encouraged" by the result of the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The government, on the other hand, is determined to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness from inflating the Poland's foreign debt, which could push it above Poland's self-imposed level of 55% of economic output, triggering austerity. The state-owned BGK bank has about 7 billion euros-8 billion euros it can sell to boost the zloty, said Rafal Benecki, senior economist at ING.\par \par \uc2 The country's debt pile is measured against the 55% limit at the end of the year, which is why \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  may intensify in December. The zloty will likely strengthen toward the end of the year, BGZ said.\par \par \uc2 -For continuously updated news from The Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 23, 2011 06:07 ET (11:07 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020111123e7bn003iq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
