\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Stocks at 6-wk lows on China; c.banks support  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 967 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 2011\par 12:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Emerging stocks at fresh six-week lows after data\par \par \uc2 * Poland, India, Singapore c.banks step in to support \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Turkey lira, bonds weaken ahead of c.bank meeting\par \par \uc2 * Egypt, Bahrain CDS surge to freshj 2-1/2 year highs\par \par \uc2 By Sujata Rao\par \par \uc2 LONDON - Emerging stocks fell 1.8 percent to six-week lows on Wednesday, battered by fresh signs of weakening growth in China, while several central banks across Asia and central Europe stepped in to support their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  versus the dollar and euro.\par \par \uc2 A slump in China's factory sector reinforced fears of a hard landing for the world's second largest economy. The data came a day after the United States cut its third quarter growth estimate, while Markit flash PMIs showed the euro zone private sector remains deep in contractionary territory, including in powerhouse Germany.\par \par \uc2 "We are still in risk aversion mode and local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are teetering. It's less about specific country fundamentals, it's a corrosion of fast-moving events encouraging deep deleveraging," said RBS strategist Imran Ahmad, referring to European banks' efforts to unwind overseas positions amid dollar funding stress and higher capital requirements.\par \par \uc2 The latest Chinese PMI was especially dismaying for markets, he said, adding: "We thought China was going to save the world (but) there are lots of cracks emerging."\par \par \uc2 The data flow fuelled a flight to safe-haven assets, weighing on emerging stocks, bonds and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost across the board, with benchmark emerging equities falling 1.8 percent\par \par \uc2 by 1040 GMT, its seventh straight session in the red. The index has shed more than 10 percent so far in November.\par \par \uc2 All major equity indices lost ground, with India leading falls in Asia, a day after its rupee \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to record lows against the dollar. Export-reliant Korean markets fell 2.3 percent after the Chinese and U.S. numbers, while the won slipped to one-month lows.\par \par \uc2 Central banks in India, Singapore and Indonesia were spotted selling dollars to buoy their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That helped the rupee rebound 0.7 percent, with some traders estimating recent Reserve Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around $4 billion.\par \par \uc2 In emerging Europe, \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to selll euros for the fourth time in less than three months, briefly helping the zloty 0.5 percent higher.\par \par \uc2 The move comes a day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deputy governor said the market situation had raised the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Stubbornly high inflation is seen forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue combating zloty weakness.\par \par \uc2 "Concerns over further \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  should curb speculation on short euro/zloty positions," a dealer in Warsaw said.\par \par \uc2 The Hungarian forint fell 0.6 percent against the euro while the Czech crown fell 0.35 percent, Both countries are seen as particularly vulnerable to deleveraging by euro zone banks.\par \par \uc2 Hungary has appealed to the International Monetary Fund for assistance but analysts are sceptical Budapest can get the kind of aid package it seeks. Failure to secure a deal could see the country lose its investment grade credit rating, fear of which pushed credit default swaps to their highest levels since 2008.\par \par \uc2 "The main risk comes from very high refinancing needs of Hungarian hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  redemptions in 2012 and 2013 in an environment where bond issuance has become more and more difficult, even for core EU17 countries," ING analysts said, noting external needs of 5.3 billion euros in 2012.\par \par \uc2 A 'disastrous' German 10-year bond auction on Wednesday raised concerns the euro zone debt crisis is even beginning to threaten Berlin.\par \par \uc2 Turkish markets were rangebound ahead of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting that is unlikely to take any concrete steps following the bank's move towards a strategy that effectively sets policy every day via overnight rates and liquidity tightening.\par \par \uc2 The lira fell a quarter point to a new one-month low against the dollar while the stock market slipped to fresh three-month lows. The benchmark yield rose 7 basis points to 10.59 percent.\par \par \uc2 The South African rand fell almost 1 percent to a two-month low against the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost 20 percent this year and is one of the world's worst performing emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rand's weakness has intensified price pressures and data on Wednesday showed annual consumer inflation quickening to 6 percent last month, at the top end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target. While the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to raise rates in the current environment, the data would appear to rule out rate cuts in the near term as well.\par \par \uc2 "... Six percent has sufficient shock value to finally erase any remnants of rate cut expectations -- we would have to see a considerable deterioration in global and South African growth to justify new easing," Standard Chartered analyst Razia Khan said.\par \par \uc2 In the Middle East, Egyptian protests entered a sixth day pushing the pound to fresh seven year highs to the dollar while stocks extended losses to a new 2-1/2 year low. The index has fallen 12 percent since protests began on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Egypt's five-year credit default swaps rose 18 bps to a fresh March 2009 high of 560, Markit said.\par \par \uc2 Unrest was also sweeping Bahrain, raising the cost of insuring debt exposure by 14 bps to 410 bps for a five-year period, the highest since May 2009, Markit data shows.\par \par \uc2 However the turmoil has failed to deter bond issuance from the Gulf with Qatar planning a bond in coming weeks. It will follow on the heels of successful issues from \uc2 Abu Dhabi Islamic Bank\uc2  while energy company Taqa and \uc2 United Arab Shipping Company\uc2  have mandated banks to manage upcoming bonds.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Carolyn Cohn; Editing by Catherine Evans)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111126e7bn0009f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
