\par\par \b \uc2 Poland's Belka Doesn't Rule Out Euro Breakup\b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 2011\par 09:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 WARSAW -- For all their determination to save the euro zone, European leaders must allow for the possibility of a breakup of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  union, Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Marek Belka, governor of the National Bank of Poland, said that in the crisis roiling Europe, no scenario can be ruled out. "For this reason, the euro zone must move forward," he said in an interview on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's news website Obserwator Finansowy.\par \par \uc2 "Many fear a two-speed Europe. I prefer a two-speed Europe than an entire Europe in stagnation," he said, referring to the idea of moving ahead with integration in the 17-nation euro zone, leaving a looser outer band of the 10 EU countries that don't use the euro.\par \par \uc2 Poland should eventually join the euro zone, but "we don't want the euro that it is today," Belka said.\par \par \uc2 As for entering the European Union's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  grid, he said that would also be unwise right now. The EU's Exchange Rate Mechanism is designed to limit volatility of national \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of euro-zone membership.\par \par \uc2 "Introducing the zloty to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  grid today is a recipe for confusion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Speculation couldn't be stopped in such a situation. Investors would wish to check if we're able to keep the zloty within a range [to the euro]," he said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since September to boost the zloty, weakened by the exit of investors from emerging markets amid the euro-zone debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 -By Marcin Sobczyk, Dow Jones Newswires; +48 22 447 2432; marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com [ 11-23-11 0355ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020111123e7bn0001d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
