\par\par \b \uc2 South African Rand Hits Fresh Two-Month Low Against Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 By Erin McCarthy   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 201 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 2011\par 15:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbled sharply Wednesday as euro-zone debt crisis worries sent investors fleeing out of riskier \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The South African rand hit a series of fresh lows, ultimately reaching its weakest level against the dollar since May 2009. The dollar rose more than 1.5% to ZAR8.5436, from ZAR8.3885 late Tuesday, according to CQG.\par \par \uc2 The Polish zloty also fell sharply, hitting a two-month low against the euro, despite an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier Wednesday by \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The euro rose to PLN4.50 against the zloty, from PLN4.4597 late Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Rising European government bond yields and a failed German bond auction Wednesday helped trigger the risk-off move, as investors remain concerned about the region's debt crisis spreading to its larger economies.\par \par \uc2 With "the new pressure in the eurozone, [emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] are really under pressure at the moment," said Guillaume Tresca, emerging market strategist at \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2  in Paris.\par \par \uc2 -By Erin McCarthy, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2712; erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com [ 23-11-11 1519GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111123e7bn000z5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
