\par\par \b \uc2 DJ MARKET TALK: European CDS Levels Unmoved After French Auction\b0\par\par\uc2 1,177 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2011\par 11:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1028 GMT [Dow Jones] European CDS levels unmoved after the French auction, with the the SovX Western Europe index eight basis points wider at 361/366 basis points, according to data-provider Markit. The iTraxx Europe index, is seven basis points wider at 190/191 basis points, while the Crossover index is 26 basis points wider at 769/774 basis points. (sarka.halasova@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1025 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/INR is trading near its intraday high, tracking a late slide in local stocks and as euro zone jitters resurface after a Spanish bond auction sees euro-era high yields; the pair is trading at 50.88 vs an intraday high of 50.92 and 50.74 late Wednesday. A dealer with a foreign bank says 51.00 is an important psychological resistance for the pair, with some traders expecting the RBI to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  around that level, but the level is "not sacrosanct" and could be broken if the EUR/USD falls below 1.3400; the pair is now trading at 1.3443. The USD/INR is not responding to local factors and is essentially a play on the euro now, he adds. The Sensex ends down 1.9%.(sudeep.jain@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1023 GMT [Dow Jones] France CDS little moved after auction at 234 bps, 9 bps wider on the day, and above the record close of 231 bps on Tuesday, according to Markit. Spain's CDS is 30 bps wider at 497 bps, also above its record close as contagion fears continue to mount. (art.patnaude@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1017 GMT [Dow Jones] Spain's CDS spread breaks a fresh high, moving 29bps wider to 496bps following the country's bond auction Thursday, Markit says. The spread breaks the record closing level of 476bps reached November 15, it notes. Spain sold EUR3.5 billion 10-year bonds at a staggering 6.66% average yield, with the maximum yield set at a euro-era high 7.088%.(serena.ruffoni@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1007 GMT [Dow Jones] Spanish bonds continue to slump after Thursday's 10-year auction priced at an average yield of 6.975%, a borrowing level considered untenable. Spain's outstanding 10-year is 35bps higher on the day while its yield spread against German bunds has hit 493bps, both euro-era highs. (nick.cawley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1006 GMT [Dow Jones] Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in a good position to defend the zloty, unless global risk aversion reaches extreme levels, according to \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2 . "We think that so far the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been successful, as the Polish authorities have maintained a strong commitment to containing the PLN's depreciation risks," SocGen says. It adds the soft line in the sand for EUR/PLN is around 4.42. In Turkey, the change in tact by the CBRT to an informal interest-rate-based strategy to contain TRY weakness has also been successful and helped the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  outperform peers, it says. EUR/PLN currently trades at 4.4354, while USD/TRY is at 1.8064.(clare.connaghan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1004 GMT [Dow Jones] Hungary needs a big rate hike, SocGen says stressing that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to be forceful and not play the "dangerous game" of implementing smaller, 50bp raises. SG says markets are expecting hikes of 200bp to 300bp from the current 6% rate, similar to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move after the \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  collapse. Given that the bank did not modify the rate when HUF reached historic lows around HUF317 vs EUR Monday, SocGen says action will come at HUF320 or higher. EUR/HUF at 313.98. (gergo.racz@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1004 GMT [Dow Jones] Thursday's Spanish bond auction was very poor, says \uc2 Rabobank\uc2 , adding this will heighten concerns that the door is closing on Spain's ability to finance itself sustainably. "This, in turn, stands to further expedite the convergence of Spanish yields with [those of] Italy...as the country plays catch-up with its more troubled peer," says Richard McGuire, senior fixed-income strategist at \uc2 Rabobank\uc2 . Spain sold EUR3.563B of the new January 2022 bond at auction Thursday, setting the maximum yield at 7.088%. (emese.bartha@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1001 GMT [Dow Jones] French 10-year bonds are eyed after the recent yield uptick says \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 . "10-year French yields are threatening to reverse the bullish trend of the last 20 years," says BarCap, adding ominously that "a Double Bottom would complete above 3.80% and target the 5.17-5.77% area." French 10-year bonds are 5ps higher at 3.745%. (nick.cawley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1000 GMT [Dow Jones] India's Sensex extends losses, and is now 2.1% lower at 16,417.80, dragged by losses in index heavyweight \uc2 Reliance Industries\uc2  (500325.BY). RIL is now down 4.7% at INR809.20. Analysts say the overall bleak market sentiment spurred selling in \uc2 Reliance Industries\uc2 , while stop-loss selling further aggravated the downside. "This is purely contagion selling," says Kishor Ostwal of \uc2 CNI Research\uc2 , adding that the stock has a strong support at INR780 and could see a sharp bounce back from there. He expects the Sensex to trade in a 16,200-17,000 band Friday. (khushita.vasant@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0956 GMT [Dow Jones] French/German 10-year yield spread eyes 200 bps as the record-breaking widening trend continues, says Francis Bray, Dow Jones Chief Technical Analyst For Europe. The 200 basis point level is a psychologically-important barrier, and this week's widening above 165.8 bps brings this 200 bps level within striking distance. Projected Fibonacci extension targets above 200 bps lie at 206.3 bps and 211.5 bps. The French/German 10-year yield spread is at 196.4 basis points. (francis.bray@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0955 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares close lower as earlier selective buying on stocks on individual cues succumb to profit-taking amid a thinly-traded market. The SET index, moved in a 992.34-999.50 range, and ended down 0.4% at 993.38. Big cap banking stocks face selling pressure as investors worry about a potential increase in non-performing loans following the country's worst flood in decades, says KGI Securities Strategist Adisak Kammool. "The market will likely move sideways in either direction until there's a fresh significant cues," he adds. Support is tipped at 990, with resistance at 999. Among top actives, \uc2 PTT Global Chemical\uc2  (PTTGC.TH) is down 1.8% at THB66.75, PTT (PTT.TH) is unchanged at THB308, Thai Oil (TOP.TH) inches up 0.4% to THB62.25, \uc2 Kasikornbank\uc2  (KBANK.TH) falls 1.7% to THB114.50, and Bangkok Bank (BBL.TH) is off 1.1% to THB141.50.(oranan.paweewun@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 17, 2011 05:28 ET (10:28 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020111117e7bh002si\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
