\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ NBP Won't Shy Away From More Zloty  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  - Belka\b0\par\par\uc2 953 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2011\par 06:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 14 Nov 2011 00:00 EDT *DJ  NBP Determined To Fight Disorderly Market Behavior In Zloty - Belka\par \par \uc2 14 Nov 2011 00:00 EDT DJ  INTERVIEW: NBP Encouraged By Result Of Zloty \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 -Belka\par \par \uc2 -- Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief reiterates NBP won't shy away from more zloty \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 -- NBP determined to fight disorderly zloty market behavior, Belka says \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Marcin Sobczyk and Gordon Fairclough \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The National Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prevent the zloty from weakening rapidly have produced an encouraging result and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is ready to step in again if investors exit the Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a disorderly fashion, said Marek Belka, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's governor.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We've shown that we wouldn't shy away from emerging in the market and the markets know that they should in their behavior take into account the risk of an NBP \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . At the same time, we've also stressed that we're not trying to defend any specific exchange rate level," he said in an exclusive interview.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "What we're determined to fight is disorderly behavior. If we see something not substantiated by global tendencies--something that is Poland-specific and unfounded, and not based on our fundamentals--then we'll step in. We've chosen a moment like this a few weeks ago and the result is encouraging for the moment," he added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The NBP \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in September to boost the zloty, weakened by the fallout of euro-zone sovereign debt concerns, when it was around PLN4.50 to the euro, bringing it to PLN4.38 within 15 minutes. It has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  twice since the original move and said its intention was to limit zloty volatility. On Friday afternoon, the zloty traded around PLN4.42 to the euro.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A catastrophic event in the euro zone, which Poland doesn't wish for, would likely weaken the zloty at first, but Poland's sound economy and proven resistance to crises could eventually prompt investors to buy the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Belka added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The immediate effect would probably be the usual one, which is the weakening of the zloty as the markets react in an instinctive way, escaping to safe havens and most liquid markets, which is the U.S. market," he said. "I wouldn't, however, assume away a reversal and an opposite movement, strengthening the zloty, because the Polish economy seems to be relatively crisis-resistant and then it will be reflected in the zloty."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "But of course we'd rather not take the risk of this tsunami. Surfing a tsunami is always a very risky business," Belka said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Marcin Sobczyk and Gordon Fairclough, Dow Jones Newswires, +48 22 447 2432;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 14 Nov 2011 00:01 EDT DJ \par INTERVIEW: NBP Encouraged By Result Of Zloty \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f