n debt concerns, when it was around PLN4.50 to the euro, bringing it to PLN4.38 within 15 minutes. It has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  twice since the original move and said its intention was to limit zloty volatility. On Friday afternoon, the zloty traded around PLN4.42 to the euro.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A catastrophic event in the euro zone, which Poland doesn't wish for, would likely weaken the zloty at first, but Poland's sound economy and proven resistance to crises could eventually prompt investors to buy the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Belka added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The immediate effect would probably be the usual one, which is the weakening of the zloty as the markets react in an instinctive way, escaping to safe havens and most liquid markets, which is the U.S. market," he said. "I wouldn't, however, assume away a reversal and an opposite movement, strengthening the zloty, because the Polish economy seems to be relatively crisis-resistant and then it will be reflected in the zloty."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "But of course we'd rather not take the risk of this tsunami. Surfing a tsunami is always a very risky business," Belka said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Marcin Sobczyk and Gordon Fairclough, Dow Jones Newswires, +48 22 447 2432;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 14 Nov 2011 00:01 EDT *DJ \par NBP Determined To Fight Disorderly Market Behavior In Zloty - Belka\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 14 Nov 2011 00:01 EDT *DJ \par NBP Won't Shy Away From More Zloty \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - Belka\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (MORE TO FOLLOW) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November 14, 2011 00:01 ET (05:01 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020111114e7be001hh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
