\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Polish cbank won't hesitate on more  \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions \highlight\uc2 -paper\b0\par\par\uc2 284 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2011\par 06:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, background)\par \par \uc2 * Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will step into \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if necessary\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are norm, not extravagance\par \par \uc2 * Needs to coordinate actions with finance ministry\par \par \uc2 (Adds background)\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Nov 14 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not hesitate to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  further in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to limit speculation, its head was quoted on Monday as saying.\par \par \uc2 The Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into the spot market three times this year -- twice in September and once in October -- to prop up the zloty, which has lost almost 10 percent of its value since the start of June on a global flight from risk.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are the absolute norm, a lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- an extravagance," Marek Belka said in an interview with daily Gazeta Wyborcza. "If we decide that further actions are necessary, we won't hesitate."\par \par \uc2 Belka added the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needed to keep the finance ministry in the loop about any potential move because the ministry could also boost the zloty by selling EU funds on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 State-owned BGK is mandated by the government to regularly convert part of the funds Poland receives from the European Union into zlotys, but it is never clear whether the bank is acting on its own account or for the finance ministry.\par \par \uc2 Polish authorities used BGK in late December to sell euros on the market, buoying the zloty ahead of the year-end fixing that determines the level of the country's public debt, almost one quarter of which is kept in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Chris Borowski and Dagmara Leszkowicz; Editing by Kim Coghill)\par \par \uc2 POLAND-CBANK/  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111117e7be00092\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
