\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Polish  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Governor: Ready To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  Again\b0\par\par\uc2 439 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Oktober 2011\par 12:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 -- Belka reiterates National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the zloty market\par \par \uc2 -- Belka says \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy should be designed for the long term\par \par \uc2 -- Poland's government should take more steps to trim budget deficit\par \par \uc2 -- Belka concerned foreign banks may scale down lending in Poland amid crisis elsewhere\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments on Poland's fiscal tightening from the sixth paragraph, on foreign-owned banks in the eighth.)\par \par \uc2 By Marcin Sobczyk\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 WARSAW (Dow Jones)--\par \par \uc2 "The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  has recently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. We decided to act when the zloty was strongly volatile and encouraged purely speculative action. We introduced an element of uncertainty to the market, hitting the expectations of potential speculators so that they don't feel unpunishable. The zloty has been more stable since then," Belka wrote.\par \par \uc2 In late September, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the zloty, weakened by the fallout of euro-zone sovereign debt concerns, when it was around PLN4.50 to the euro. It has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice since the original \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . At 0845 GMT Monday, the zloty was at PLN4.26 to the euro.\par \par \uc2 Belka also said stability of monetary policy was important for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which left its interest rates unchanged at the October meeting after raising rates four times earlier this year to bring elevated consumer price inflation down. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will fight inflation, but not in an erratic way, "by tightening the screws too much in order to loosen them too much soon after," he said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark rate is at 4.5%, while Poland's inflation in September fell to 3.9% on the year after peaking at 5% in May.\par \par \uc2 The Polish government, recently reelected for a second four-year term in power, should continue fiscal consolidation to earn Poland a higher credit rating than its current A-, Belka also wrote. Poland plans to cut its general government deficit from 7.9% at the end of 2010 to 2.9% at the end of 2012.\par \par \uc2 The government should make "another meaningful step" to cut the deficit to demonstrate to the markets "that the Polish budget gap is being narrowed and borrowing needs are in check," Belka said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor also said the ongoing financial crisis may force foreign banks to limit lending, which may impact the Polish banks they own.\par \par \uc2 Full report: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bbwp.pl/artykul/marek-belka-polska-zasluguje-na-wiecej/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.bbwp.pl/artykul/marek-belka-polska-zasluguje-na-wiecej/ }}}\par \par \uc2 -By Marcin Sobczyk, Dow Jones Newswires; +48 22 447 2432; marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com [ 17-10-11 1044GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111017e7ah000q5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
